RF.put("questb:b41",{"8521":{"id":8521,"t":"The Alliance Needs More Silk Bandages!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 20 silk bandages to Nurse Stonefield at the airfield in Dun Morogh.\n20 Silk Bandage","desc":"It is very kind of you to offer to help me again ‹class›. It looks like we've collected $2082w silk bandages, so we'll need more.","rew":"You will receive:\n5 Alliance Commendation Signet Ahn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","back":"It is very kind of you to offer to help me again, ‹class›. It looks like we've collected a goodly number of the silk bandages we've been tasked with, but we still need more. ‹name›, is there any way that you could see fit to put together another bundle and return them to me here? The Alliance and I will be most grateful.","done":"You are such a selfless person. Thank you very much for your contribution to the war effort. It's people like you that are going to make the difference between success and failure at Ahn'Qiraj. I just hope that all of this will be enough.\nThanks again, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":59.9,"y":33.6,"n":"Nurse Stonefield","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"8601":{"id":8601,"t":"The Horde Needs More Rugged Leather!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 10 Rugged Leather to Doctor Serratus at the Valley of Spirits in Orgrimmar.\n10 Rugged Leather sold by Lhara","desc":"Preparations for the impending war at Ahn'Qiraj are proceeding, ‹class›. However, to ensure that we do not fall behind, or at least that I am not the one that causes us to fall behind, I want for you to bring back another stack of rugged leather. Your prompt attention to this matter will be greatly appreciated, ‹name›.","rew":"You will receive:\n10 Horde Commendation Signet Ahn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","done":"Practice, practice, practice. A well honed knife and the skill to use it will get you far in this world, ‹name›. Looks like the edges on these skins are better than the last. Did you buy a new knife?\nIn any case, we thank you for your efforts. Your donation has been noted, and will be put to good use I can assure you. Should you find yourself in the possession of more rugged leather, be sure to come back and speak with me, as I will probably need it.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":35.2,"y":72.5,"n":"Doctor Serratus","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"7081":{"id":7081,"t":"Alterac Valley Graveyards","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays 90s instead of 0.","obj":"Assault a graveyard, then return to Sergeant Durgen Stormpike in the Alterac Mountains.\nGraveyard Assaulted","desc":"The graveyards in Alterac Valley are prized territories. Both the Horde and the Alliance fight savagely for these sacred grounds. Are you, ‹name›, ready to join that fight?\nI want you to assault an enemy graveyard. Find a graveyard with a Horde banner in its midst, and pull it from the ground! Do that, and your task will be complete....\nBut if you can also hold the graveyard for a few minutes, then our troops will soon come to relieve you.","rew":"Money: 90 0 gold, 90 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Stormpike Guard\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"‹name›, you have not yet assaulted a graveyard. Return to me when this task is complete!","done":"Well done! Graveyards are vital to our control of Alterac Valley. When you capture one, you help ensure the Alliance's sovereignty here.\nGo now, ‹name›. Reenter the battle, and if you see a graveyard under the Horde's control... you know what to do!","pins":[{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":36.8,"y":77.2,"n":"Sergeant Durgen Stormpike","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["alterac-valley"]},"7001":{"id":7001,"t":"Empty Stables","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Locate a Frostwolf in Alterac Valley. Use the Frostwolf Muzzle when you are near the Frostwolf to 'tame' the beast. Once tamed, the Frostwolf will follow you back to the Frostwolf Stable Master. Speak with the Frostwolf Stable Master to earn credit for the capture.\nProvided: Frostwolf Muzzle","desc":"The war in the valley has taken its toll on our soldiers. We must revitalize our forces!\nIf we can fill up the stables, the Wolf Riders will once more be able to ride out into the field of battle.\nTake this muzzle and track down the frostwolves that inhabit the nearby forest. Once you find a wolf, use the muzzle to tame the beast. Bring the tamed beast back to me so that I may place it in the stable.\nWhen we have enough wolves stabled, the Wolf Riders will rejoin their patrol on our front lines.","back":"Without your help, the Frostwolf Wolf Riders would not have mounts to ride into battle. You do us a great service!","done":"I can only hope that those charged with collecting ram hides are as determined as you, ‹name›.\nAt this rate, we will have the stables full in a matter of hours!\nStart Frostwolf Stable Master Alterac Valley End Frostwolf Stable Master Alterac Valley Level 60 , requires level 51 Difficulty 51 56 58 Side Horde Shareable No Repeatable Yes Quest ID 7001","cats":["alterac-valley"]},"7241":{"id":7241,"t":"In Defense of Frostwolf","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Venture to Alterac Valley, located in the Alterac Mountains. Find and speak with Warmaster Laggrond - who stands outside the tunnel entrance - to begin your career as a soldier of Frostwolf. You will find Alterac Valley north of Tarren Mill at the base of the Alterac Mountains.","desc":"The drums of war sound off in a distant land, ‹class›. The favored clan of your Warchief is under attack from the nefarious Stormpike Guard of Ironforge.\nBy the looks of you, I can discern that you are indeed battle hardy and prepared to take on the cause of the Frostwolf.\nIt is you who must now take the next step in your evolution.\nNorth of Tarren Mill, in Alterac, you will find the entrance to Alterac Valley. It is there that you will find Warmaster Laggrond. Hurry ‹class›, for the battle is upon us!","rew":"Experience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Frostwolf Clan\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","done":"To become a soldier of Frostwolf, one must first be tested...\nOrgrimmar Alterac Mountains","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":49.6,"y":71.2,"n":"Frostwolf Ambassador Rokhstrom","s":1},{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":62.3,"y":58.9,"n":"Warmaster Laggrond","e":1}],"cats":["alterac-valley"]},"7161":{"id":7161,"t":"Proving Grounds","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to the Wildpaw cavern located southeast of the main base in Alterac Valley and find the Frostwolf Banner. Return the Frostwolf Banner to Warmaster Laggrond.\nFrostwolf Banner Frostwolf Banner in Alterac Valley","desc":"Hail, ‹class›. It has been a long time since we have had the chance to answer the call of battle. The old feelings are slow to rise but once awakened, the blood does rush. The battle rage returns...\nAll newcomers to the Valley must first complete the rite of battle.\nDeep within the Wildpaw gnoll cave is a banner of the Frostwolf. Venture forth and recover the banner. Return it to me and I shall grant you the Frostwolf initiate's insignia.","rew":"You will receive:\nFrostwolf Insignia Rank 1 Peeling the Onion\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Frostwolf Clan\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Wake up! Wake up, ‹name›! This is not a dream. You really are entrenched in the midst of a raging battle!","done":"That burning sensation you feel is your soul being awakened. Your spirit has accepted the call to arms.\nYou are now one of the Frostwolf, ‹name›. Congratulations.\nCarry this insignia with you at all times. As you advance among the ranks of Frostwolf, I will replace the insignia with other, more powerful insignias.\nPerhaps someday you will be exalted among the Frostwolf Clan. Should that day ever come, you will be granted the Eye of Command.","pins":[{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":62.3,"y":58.9,"n":"Warmaster Laggrond","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["alterac-valley"]},"7401":{"id":7401,"t":"Wanted: DWARVES!","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"You have been tasked with slaying opposing Dwarf players in Alterac Valley.\nKill a Dwarf and rip out their spine. Take the Dwarf Spine to Sergeant Yazra Bloodsnarl at Frostwolf Keep.\nDwarf Spine Alliance Sentinel , Stormpike Mountaineer , Frostwolf in Alterac Valley , Snowblind Harpy in Alterac Valley and 4 more","desc":"By order of Sergeant Yazra Bloodsnarl, all dwarves on the field of battle are to be killed on sight.\nShould you slay a dwarf in combat, rip out their spine, leaving a spineless heap of stink and rot to serve as a warning to any and all that dare oppose the might of the Frostwolf.\nReturn to Sergeant Yazra Bloodsnarl with proof of your heroics.","rew":"Money: 1 80 1 gold, 80 silver, 0 copper Experience: 9,550","back":"I deal in wholesale irony, soldier.","done":"You now have license to decimate dwarves by the dozen, ‹class›!\n<Yazra stares off into the distance for a moment.>\nYou never forget your first de-spining...\nStart Wanted: DWARVES! Alterac Valley Level 60 , requires level 51 Difficulty 51 56 58 Side Horde Type PvP Shareable Yes Quest ID 7401","cats":["alterac-valley"]},"8441":{"id":8441,"t":"Conquering Arathi Basin","lv":49,"min":40,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 3 Arathi Basin Mark of Honor to a Horde Warbringer outside the battlegrounds.\n3 Arathi Basin Mark of Honor","desc":"Our conflict with the Alliance has escalated to a true war. No longer are false pretenses to enter into battle used or expected by either side at this point.\nThe battle for the Arathi Basin is one of resources, plain and simple. Either the Alliance gets the resources and uses them against us or we get them and use them to keep our war efforts going. Help the Defilers maintain the flow of resources we need, ‹name›!","rew":"Experience: 2,250\n+50 reputation with The Defilers","back":"You've come back with news from Arathi, ‹class›?","done":"Securing our resources in Arathi is an important task! You've done well, ‹name›.\nThe Barrens Arathi Highlands Undercity","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":46.7,"y":8.7,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":73.5,"y":29.1,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":58.3,"y":97.9,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["arathi-basin"]},"8121":{"id":8121,"t":"Take Four Bases","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Hold four bases at the same time in Arathi Basin, and then return to Deathmaster Dwire in Hammerfall.","desc":"‹name›, as the battles over Arathi Basin rage, news of your actions have reached many ears. You are highly regarded among us, which gives me confidence that you will accomplish the mission I now have for you.\nIt is time to send a message to the League of Arathor. We must show them that their holdings in Arathi Basin are tenuous and quickly lost. We will show them this by holding, all at once, four strategic points in Arathi Basin.\nSucceed in this, ‹name›, and earn great respect among the Defilers.","rew":"Money: 2 70 2 gold, 70 silver, 0 copper Experience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with The Defilers\n+200 reputation with The Defilers\n+200 reputation with The Defilers\n+200 reputation with The Defilers","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":73.3,"y":29.7,"n":"Deathmaster Dwire","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["arathi-basin"]},"681":{"id":681,"t":"Northfold Manor","lv":31,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 10 Syndicate Highwaymen and 6 Syndicate Mercenaries.\nReturn to Captain Nials at Refuge Pointe.\nSyndicate Highwayman slain : 0/ 10\nSyndicate Mercenary slain : 0/ 6","desc":"We are fighting a war for Stromgarde, and we are losing. The ogres, the Syndicate and we have divided our once great city, and each faction battles the other into a bloody stalemate.\nBut our forces dwindle while our enemy grows.\nWe need help from the town of Southshore, but supplies are difficult to receive while the Syndicate holds territory between us.\nGo to the Syndicate base in Northfold Manor and slay them. Then, perhaps, pressure on our supply trains will lessen and more will get through.","rew":"Experience: 2,500\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"‹name›, with each passing hour our hold on Stromgarde grows more tenuous. You must make haste or our city will surely fall.","done":"Very good, ‹name›. With the deaths of those Syndicate members we should have an easier time receiving supplies from Southshore.\nPerhaps our cause yet has hope.","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":45.8,"y":47.6,"n":"Captain Nials","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["arathi-highlands"]},"6441":{"id":6441,"t":"Satyr Horns","lv":26,"min":21,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Collect 16 Satyr Horns for Pixel in Splintertree Post.\n16 Satyr Horns Geltharis 50 % , Caedakar the Vicious 50 % , Balizar the Umbrage 50 % , Aligar the Tormentor 50 % and 4 more","desc":"Heya! I've been traveling through Ashenvale, heading towards Ratchet, and decided to make a stop here at Splintertree. I'm always looking for an opportunity, and it seems that satyr horns are in high demand in Ratchet these days.\nAfter asking around here, it seems that the satyrs in Night Run, Satyrnaar, and Xavian all have the type of horns I am looking for. I'm no match for those satyrs... but you look like you might be!\nTell you what, you collect the horns for me and I'll make it worth your time.","rew":"Money: 20 0 gold, 20 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,100\n+100 reputation with Ratchet","back":"I hope you can be quick about getting those horns, ‹name›. I'm heading back to Ratchet soon!","done":"These are perfect, ‹name›! Thanks for helping me out!\nOh, and this is for your time...","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":73.1,"y":61.5,"n":"Pixel","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"3561":{"id":3561,"t":"Delivery to Archmage Xylem","lv":52,"min":45,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Tablet of Sael'hai to Archmage Xylem in Azshara.\nTablet of Sael'hai Tablet of Sael'hai\nProvided: Tablet of Sael'hai","desc":"This final tablet goes to someone very dangerous, ‹name›. Heed me when I tell you that I trust this person far less than anyone else I've asked you to meet with.\nArchmage Xylem has a tower up in the hills overlooking Azshara. He's human, but he acts like no human I've met... or killed. He exudes power, and I dare not ask him what he plans on doing with the tablet.\nHe came to me, but told me that his bodyguard Sanath would help me get to the tower when I was ready to meet him. Look north for Sanath.","rew":"Money: 40 0 gold, 40 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,550","back":"What can help you with, ‹name›?","done":"Ah, the Tablet of Sael'hai... how long I've longed to study it.\nThank you, ‹name›. You may tell Jediga that she has done well. This will definitely be worth the payment she asked for.","pins":[{"z":"Azshara","x":22.6,"y":51.4,"n":"Jediga","s":1},{"z":"Azshara","x":29.2,"y":40.2,"n":"Archmage Xylem","e":1}],"cats":["azshara"]},"6921":{"id":6921,"t":"Amongst the Ruins","lv":27,"min":21,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 6,550 experience instead of 2,750, 2.38 times as much. Read from what the game server sent.","obj":"Bring the Fathom Core to Je'neu Sancrea at Zoram'gar Outpost, Ashenvale.\nFathom Core Fathom Stone","desc":"The Twilight's Hammer has moved into the Moonshrine Ruins of Blackfathom Deeps. Their presence can only serve to coerce the elements into working against us. If left unchecked, this region will be theirs for good.\n‹name›, go into Blackfathom and find the ruin's fathom stone; it should be somewhere close in the water. In it is a fathom core - a device that when properly read it will relate a history of all elemental activity. If I have it, I and the Earthen Ring can maybe do something to stop them!","rew":"Money: 45 0 gold, 45 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,550\n+150 reputation with Darkspear Trolls\n+150 reputation with Earthen Ring","back":"Have you been successful in locating the fathom core? Without it we'll have no idea what the Twilight's Hammer is exactly up to down there.","done":"This is exactly what I need! A fathom core is an incredible well of information that we will be able to draw much good from. Whatever the Twilight's Hammer is up to in there - and believe me when I say it is no good - my comrades and I will now uncover.\nYou've done well here today; the Earthen Ring looks upon you warmly for assisting us. You've also helped the Horde as a whole, and for that you should be proud.","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":11.6,"y":34.3,"n":"Je'neu Sancrea","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blackfathom-deeps"]},"3801":{"id":3801,"t":"Dark Iron Legacy","lv":52,"min":48,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Franclorn Forgewright if you are interested in obtaining a key to the city major.","desc":"Greetings, ‹name›. I am Franclorn Forgewright. Yes, the Franclorn Forgewright responsible for the stonewrought method of architecture. You have undoubtedly passed through or stood upon one of my creations in your adventures across our war torn world.\nYou are probably wondering why I am here and what it is that I want from you - both valid questions.\nI need your assistance, of course. In exchange for your assistance, I shall grant you the key to the depths of my accursed city.","rew":"Experience: 500","done":"Whether it is greed which brought you here or an act of selfless devotion, what you are about to undertake is for the good of us all.","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":29,"y":28.9,"n":"Franclorn Forgewright","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blackrock-depths"]},"4201":{"id":4201,"t":"The Love Potion","lv":54,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 4 Gromsblood, 10 Giant Silver Veins and Nagmara's Filled Vial to Mistress Nagmara in Blackrock Depths.\n4 Gromsblood Gromsblood , Gromsblood , El Pollo Grande 28.6 % , Treant Spirit 3 % and 4 more\n10 Giant Silver Vein Cliff Walker 80 % , Cliff Thunderer 80 % , Cliff Breaker 80 %\nNagmara's Filled Vial\nProvided: Nagmara's Vial","desc":"Oh, the pains of love! My dear Private Rocknot is immune to my charms. I am spurned! It's maddening!\nYou must help me! We succubi know much of love, and I can make a potion to beat down the iron walls around Rocknot's heart. To make it, I need these items: the herb gromsblood, giant silver veins from the cliff giants of Azshara, and water from the Golakka Springs Crater in Un'Goro. You can place the water in this vial.\nPlease, ‹name›, help a poor soul in her quest for happiness!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nManacle Cuffs Nagmara's Whipping Belt\nMoney: 80 0 gold, 80 silver, 0 copper Experience: 5,450","back":"Do you have the ingredients? The hole in my heart threatens to consume me!","done":"Oh, you've done it! I can now make my potion and use it on Rocknot. Finally, he will fall victim to my charms!\nThank you, ‹name›. You are a champion of love!\nAzshara Open the zone on the world map Start Mistress Nagmara End Mistress Nagmara Level 54 , requires level 50 Difficulty 50 52 57 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Type Dungeon Shareable No Quest ID 4201","cats":["blackrock-depths"]},"4121":{"id":4121,"t":"Precarious Predicament","lv":58,"min":52,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Escort your prisoner, Grark Lorkrub, through Burning Steppes and through Blackrock Mountain to the Searing Gorge.\nYou recall Lexlort mentioning that he would have his men waiting on the other side to take Grark into custody.\nYou will also be required to hand over your Thorium Shackles to Lexlort.\nThorium Shackles","desc":"Do you truly believe that you will make it to your rendezvous point with me in custody? You actually expected to break into a heavily fortified Blackrock fortress to capture a prized asset of theirs without alerting anyone or anything to your presence?\nYou will be destroyed!","rew":"Money: 2 65 2 gold, 65 silver, 0 copper Experience: 7,750\n+150 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"I will take this traitorous filth, ‹name›.","done":"Your heroics will not go unrecognized, ‹name›. You have earned this tribute. The Warlord will speak with you now in regards to the final mission.\nBurning Steppes Badlands","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":40.2,"y":34.2,"n":"Grark Lorkrub","s":1},{"z":"Badlands","x":5.9,"y":47.6,"n":"Lexlort","e":1}],"cats":["blackrock-depths"]},"4361":{"id":4361,"t":"The Bearer of Bad News","lv":59,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return to Ironforge and deliver the bad news to King Magni Bronzebeard.","desc":"You must take this information back to King Magni, ‹name›. He will know what to do!","rew":"Experience: 6,400","done":"<King Magni slams his fist down in anger.>","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":57.4,"y":30.1,"n":"King Magni Bronzebeard","e":1}],"cats":["blackrock-depths"]},"5001":{"id":5001,"t":"Bijou's Belongings","lv":59,"min":55,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Bijou's Belongings and return them to her. Good luck!\nBijou's Belongings Bijou's Belongings","desc":"Ordinarily I don't deal with ‹race›s but it seems that I'm stuck between a troll and a hard place. You see, my mission here is one of utmost importance to the Horde. The information I've discovered, however, applies to the well being of the Alliance as well. Now believe me, I'm no Alliance sympathizer, but the Blackrock threat is bigger than just a bunch of orcs.\nYou help me out by finding my belongings and I'll help you out with some information that could prove useful to your kind.\nDeal?","rew":"Experience: 6,400","back":"Any luck?","done":"Well I'll be! Where were they??\nStart Bijou End Bijou Level 59 , requires level 55 Difficulty 55 57 Side Alliance Type Dungeon Shareable Yes Quest ID 5001\nThe chain\n3 quests from level 59 to 60, 21,100 XP in all.\n1 [ 59 ] Bijou's Belongings this quest\nFind Bijou's Belongings and return them to her.\nBijou\n6,400 XP\n2 [ 59 ] Message to Maxwell\nTravel to the Burning Steppes and give Bijou's Information to Marshal Maxwell.\nBijou\n6,400 XP\n3 [ 60 ] Maxwell's Mission\nTravel to Blackrock Spire and destroy War Master Voone, Highlord Omokk, and Overlord Wyrmthalak.\nMarshal Maxwell Burning Steppes\n8,300 XP","cats":["blackrock-spire"]},"5081":{"id":5081,"t":"Maxwell's Mission","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 8,300 experience instead of 8,550, 0.97 times as much.","obj":"Travel to Blackrock Spire and destroy War Master Voone, Highlord Omokk, and Overlord Wyrmthalak. Return to Marshal Maxwell when the job is done.\nWar Master Voone slain\nHighlord Omokk slain\nOverlord Wyrmthalak slain","desc":"This information fills in the gaps to our otherwise impeccable intelligence of Blackrock Spire.\nThe attack must be decisive, ‹name›.\nFirst their war master, the troll Voone, must be destroyed. Without his battle plans, the Blackrock orcs will be thrown into chaos.\nYou must then take out the ogre Highlord, Omokk. The cowardly ogres of Blackrock are powerless without his leadership.\nLastly, the overlord of the citadel: Wyrmthalak. With Wyrmthalak dead, their central command unit is without a conduit.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nWyrmthalak's Shackles Omokk's Girth Restrainer Halycon's Muzzle Vosh'gajin's Strand Voone's Vice Grips\nMoney: 1 80 1 gold, 80 silver, 0 copper Experience: 8,300\n+150 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Status?","done":"Excellent work, ‹name›. At the very least, you have bought us more time - precious, precious time.","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":84.7,"y":69,"n":"Marshal Maxwell","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blackrock-spire"]},"2761":{"id":2761,"t":"Smelt On, Smelt Off","lv":45,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring forty Mithril Bars and forty Iron Bars to Galvan the Ancient in Stranglethorn.\n40 Iron Bar\n40 Mithril Bar","desc":"Many blacksmiths believe that mining and smithing are separate, independent jobs; but can there be blacksmithing without mining? Ah ha -- it is an impossibility! The accomplished blacksmith must also be an accomplished miner.\nShow Galvan that you are capable, ‹name›. Bring me forty bars of iron and forty bars of mithril. For this, Galvan will teach you the ways of the ornate mithril pants!","rew":"You will receive:\nPlans: Ornate Mithril Pants\nExperience: 3,900","back":"After such mining, your muscles bulge and your body aches!","done":"Your work ethic is impeccable, ‹name›! You are starting to understand the ways of Galvan mineralogy! Take this and learn from it all that you can.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":50.6,"y":20.5,"n":"Galvan the Ancient","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blacksmithing"]},"3321":{"id":3321,"t":"Did You Lose This?","lv":50,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 7,100 experience instead of 6,934, 1.02 times as much.","obj":"Wait for Trenton to finish his work.","desc":"You have done much for the Order, ‹name›. The sheer dedication it takes to get this far would have turned away any ordinary person. There is no doubt in my mind, or in the mind of Galvan, that you are one of us.\nWhich is why I think you deserve a little reward. It is nothing really, just a trinket. You may be familiar with its properties, as I do believe it is what brought you to us in the first place.","rew":"You will receive:\nGlimmering Mithril Insignia\nExperience: 7,100","back":"Today we finalize our celebration of your commitment to the Order.","done":"Rise and be recognized, ‹name›, blacksmith of the Mithril Order.","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":51.4,"y":28.8,"n":"Trenton Lighthammer","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blacksmithing"]},"2601":{"id":2601,"t":"The Basilisk's Bite","lv":50,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring ten Basilisk Brains and two Vulture Gizzards to Bloodmage Lynnore.\n10 Basilisk Brain Redstone Basilisk 40 % , Redstone Crystalhide 40 % , Deatheye 30 %\n2 Vulture Gizzard Black Slayer 40 % , Spiteflayer 30 %","desc":"These wastelands are riddled with redstone basilisk, ‹name›. These basilisk have adapted and flourished, more so than any of the other wildlife within the region.\nI have watched from afar as they hunt and go about their daily activities - the beasts exhibit a thought process more complex than even some humanoids.\nI must study their brains!\nRetrieve ten of their brains for me, ‹name›. The compound cannot be complete, however, without two vulture gizzards to form the base of the solution.","rew":"You will receive:\nCerebral Cortex Compound\nExperience: 4,700","back":"Have you returned with the requested organs?","done":"This is wondrous, ‹name›! My offering to you is a taste of the inner workings of the redstone basilisk.\nShould the compound be to your liking, more can always be made... for a price.","pins":[{"z":"Blasted Lands","x":50.6,"y":14.3,"n":"Bloodmage Lynnore","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blasted-lands"]},"2521":{"id":2521,"t":"To Serve Kum'isha","lv":55,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"In your journeys throughout the Blasted Lands, should you ever come across a Flawless Draenethyst Sphere, take the item back to Kum'isha the Collector.\nBe warned, this gem is one of the most rare crystals in all of Azeroth. Any creature in these lands could be holding a Flawless Draenethyst Sphere.\nYou will be rewarded for each Flawless Draenethyst Sphere you have collected.\nFlawless Draenethyst Sphere Teremus the Devourer , Bonepicker 0 % , Felcular 0 % , Ilifar 0 % and 4 more","desc":"‹race›, can your miniscule brain comprehend the rarity of a flawless sphere of draenethyst? Draenei have spent lifetimes in search of just one of these crystals, only to meet horrible fates, their purpose unfulfilled.\nSo you stand before Kum'isha, knowing what Kum'isha has requested and still wish to assist? Very well, ‹race›... At any time during your travels across these lands, should you find a flawless sphere of draenethyst, return it to me and I shall reward you with riches beyond your wildest dreams.","rew":"You will receive:\nEmerald Encrusted Chest\nExperience: 8,450","back":"I have dedicated my life to the search of flawless draenethyst spheres. A lifetime, ‹race›!","done":"Do my eyes deceive me? Impossible! Where did you... How...\nPerhaps now a rift can be opened, returning us to our homeland.","pins":[{"z":"Blasted Lands","x":52,"y":35.6,"n":"Kum'isha the Collector","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blasted-lands"]},"2681":{"id":2681,"t":"The Stones That Bind Us","lv":57,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Free nine Servants of Razelikh, three Servants of Sevine, three Servants of Allistarj, and three Servants of Grol. Return to the Fallen Hero when your task is complete. You must remain within close proximity of the stones or the process will fail.\nServants of Razelikh Freed : 0/ 9\nServants of Grol Freed : 0/ 3\nServants of Allistarj Freed : 0/ 3\nServants of Sevine Freed : 0/ 3","desc":"It will take more than you alone to overcome the forces of Razelikh and his subordinates.\nGather a suitable group of adventurers and free my men of their eternal torture! Eighteen stones you must shatter.\nFight hard and die with honor, ‹name›.","rew":"Experience: 7,550","back":"It is no easy task, ‹name›. Do not give up!","done":"You have done it, ‹name›! The poor, tortured souls can finally rest.\nOur work is not yet over, ‹name›. We have much to discuss and much more to accomplish.\nSwamp of Sorrows Blasted Lands","pins":[{"z":"Swamp of Sorrows","x":34.3,"y":66.1,"n":"Fallen Hero of the Horde","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blasted-lands"]},"97961":{"id":97961,"t":"Camping 101 tailoring","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Bowen Brisboise on the road to Brill from Deathknell to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your tailoring skill to 20","desc":"Tailoring is a surprisingly potent tradeskill to invest in, and I'm sure it'll serve you well.\nI know someone that can teach you how to craft a Faction Banner for your camp, provided you have the skill for it. Inspiration and morale are a key part of success on any battlefield, and an inspirational banner can go a long way to keeping you energized.","done":"There you have it, you can now craft your very own Rallying Banner. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":57.2,"y":55.4,"n":"Eleanor Shackleton","s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":52.6,"y":55.6,"n":"Bowen Brisboise","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"7321":{"id":7321,"t":"Soothing Turtle Bisque","lv":31,"min":28,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 10 pieces of Turtle Meat and some Soothing Spices to Christoph Jeffcoat in Tarren Mill.\n10 Turtle Meat Giant Surf Glider 53 % , Coralshell Tortoise 46.7 % , Saltwater Snapjaw 40.8 % , Mudrock Tortoise 40.6 % and 4 more\nSoothing Spices sold by Gunder Thornbush , sold by Banalash , sold by Nerrist , sold by Edna Mullby and 4 more","desc":"Who says that the undead don't know anything about cooking? Take my secret recipe for Turtle Bisque, for example. I've known folks that would come back from the dead just to enjoy a bowl! Heh, heh...\nSpeaking of which, I haven't been able to make any lately. I used to head over to Lake Lordamere myself to hunt snapjaws, the nasty things, but I can't pull myself away from my work here.\nIf you bring me some Turtle Meat from the snapjaws and soothing spices, I'll show you how it's done!","rew":"You will receive:\nRecipe: Soothing Turtle Bisque 3 Soothing Turtle Bisque\nMoney: 30 0 gold, 30 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,500\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"Any luck finding the ingredients? I'll tell you, the alliance maggots are far too numerous in this area now... In my opinion, they have come far too close already...","done":"My soothing turtle bisque will keep you warm on a cold night... if you care about that kind of thing.\nHillsbrad Foothills Alterac Mountains","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":62.3,"y":19,"n":"Christoph Jeffcoat","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["cooking"]},"94281":{"id":94281,"t":"Craftsmans writ advanced target dummy","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Advanced Target Dummy\nAdvanced Target Dummy","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Advanced Target Dummy, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Advanced Target Dummy Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94281","cats":["crafting"]},"7881":{"id":7881,"t":"Carnival Boots","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"3 Embossed Leather Boots","rew":"You will receive:\nDarkmoon Faire Prize Ticket\n+100 reputation with Darkmoon Faire","back":"We at the Darkmoon Faire do much walking. We walk from one faire site to another... in fact, you'll never see us sitting down on the job! So it is no surprise that we wear out quite a lot of boots! We need boots that are both durable and stylish, and embossed leather boots fit that bill rather well.\nYou! You're a leatherworker; make me embossed leather boots and I'll give you a Darkmoon Faire ticket for the work.","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. These are quite well made. The craftsmanship is top notch! Here is a Darkmoon Faire ticket... enjoy, sir.\nElwynn Forest Mulgore","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":43.6,"y":70.8,"n":"Chronos","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Mulgore","x":37.2,"y":42.5,"n":"Chronos","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkmoon-faire"]},"1001":{"id":1001,"t":"Buzzbox 411","lv":12,"min":7,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Collect 3 Thresher Eyes from Darkshore Threshers in the deep sea near Buzzbox 411.\n3 Thresher Eye Darkshore Thresher 40 % , Elder Darkshore Thresher 40 %","desc":"A tiny voice crackles from deep within the machine.\n\"Wizbang here! The next Buzzbox is north of Auberdine, on the beach\nSo, that Buzzbox is number 411 and it needs 3 Thresher Eyes for its repairs. They're just off the coast! The darkshore threshers... *Hic*... Sorry about that...\nJust like last time, when you give the Buzzbox the goods, it'll spit out your reward. *Hic*... What? No, I'm fine!\"","rew":"Money: 10 0 gold, 10 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,150\n+150 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"The machine's hatch is open and it seems to wait expectantly for 3 Thresher Eyes to be placed inside.","done":"The Buzzbox hums to life soon after you place the Thresher Eyes inside. There is a moment of static before you hear a familiar tiny voice call out.\n\"Crawler wine is the best...\" *hic*\n\"What? Oh, you fixed it already? Wow, you're a fasht one. Sho, would ya like to fix another?\"\nYou believe you hear a liquid being poured into a cup, followed by loud gulping sounds.","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":36.6,"y":46.3,"n":"Buzzbox 827","s":1},{"z":"Darkshore","x":42,"y":28.6,"n":"Buzzbox 411","e":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"4681":{"id":4681,"t":"Washed Ashore","lv":14,"min":11,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Recover the Sea Turtle Remains from the Skeletal Sea Turtle in the waters west of Auberdine, and then speak with Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde back in Auberdine.\nSea Turtle Remains Skeletal Sea Turtle","desc":"That beached creature is not an isolated incident here in Darkshore. There are more along the coastline and even in the water. I would like for you to investigate another one that we know of; this one was reported to be in the water due west of Auberdine, close to a sunken vessel. Return to me with anything that you may recover that would aid our research.\nAlso, in your travels you may find other creatures. By all means, if you should discover anything then please bring it to our attention!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nSandcomber Boots Dryweed Belt Clamshell Bracers\nExperience: 975\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Once you have investigated the creature's remains in the water to the west of here, I should be able to file a proper report with the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus. Perhaps then we will be closer to discovering the reason why these unfortunate creatures choose to end their lives beached on the coast of Darkshore.","done":"You've been a tremendous help here today; we now have a solid chance at unlocking the mystery of why these creatures choose to beach themselves on the cost of Darkshore. The idea that they might be fleeing the area around Teldrassil is disturbing. Should you come across others in your travels, please let me know. Our research here is but in its infancy.\nOn behalf of the Temple of the Moon, please accept this as thanks for the effort you have given. Thank you, ‹name›!","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":36.6,"y":45.6,"n":"Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"4761":{"id":4761,"t":"Thundris Windweaver","lv":15,"min":11,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Thundris Windweaver in Auberdine.","desc":"Your scouting of the furbolg camp is information that Thundris Windweaver should be made aware of. He graciously serves as the elder of Auberdine, offering sage and just stewardship of the day to day affairs of the village. Please - share with him your findings to date on the furbolg situation.\nI believe he has some ideas of his own on the reasons behind their corruption. Perhaps you can work with him to enact a plan to restore the balance of nature here!","rew":"Experience: 110\n+10 reputation with Darnassus","done":"Well met, ‹class›. Your scouting of the furbolg situation comes at a fortuitous time for us in Auberdine. For some time we have dealt with not only forest dwellers who are now openly hostile to our presence, but also the outright corruption of the forest itself. Hopefully you might be able to lend Auberdine aid during these troubling times.","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":39.4,"y":43.5,"n":"Terenthis","s":1},{"z":"Darkshore","x":37.4,"y":40.1,"n":"Thundris Windweaver","e":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"5321":{"id":5321,"t":"The Sleeper Has Awakened","lv":20,"min":17,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. New rewards: Deerhide Pants.","obj":"Escort Kerlonian Evershade to Liladris Moonriver south along the road to find his bag in Darkshore.\nHorn of Awakening\nKerlonian Evershade slain\nEscort Kerlonian Evershade on the road south to his bag","desc":"I was on my way to Maestra's Post to meet Liladris Moonriver, but I decided to stop here and take a short nap. Ever since I awoke from the emerald dream, I have been so sleepy...\n<yawn>\nAnd I can't find my things anywhere! Would you mind helping me find them?\nI understand that Maestra's Post is south of here, along the road in Ashenvale. I had come from that way...\nLastly, I may fall asleep so if you ever need to wake me, please use my horn. You'll find it in the chest here.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nOwlsight Rifle Jadefinger Baton Steelcap Shield Deerhide Pants\nNew in Forever: Deerhide Pants.\nExperience: 1,550\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Has Kerlonian arrived?","done":"Oh, I am so happy Kerlonian made it! And I'm sure I'll find him sleeping somewhere around here, won't I?\nThank you for showing him the way, ‹name›.\nDarkshore Ashenvale","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":44.4,"y":76.4,"n":"Kerlonian Evershade","s":1},{"z":"Ashenvale","x":27.3,"y":35.6,"n":"Liladris Moonriver","e":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"6761":{"id":6761,"t":"The New Frontier","lv":55,"min":54,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Mathrengyl Bearwalker at the Cenarion Enclave of Darnassus.","desc":"I have relegated my second, Mathrengyl Bearwalker, to deal with Moonglade's call for aid. Speak to him on this matter - NOT me.\nLet me give you some... friendly... advice. It is I who led us out of the darkness - NOT the Cenarion Circle in Moonglade - when all was lost for our race. Teldrassil gives us all new life! They would have you believe otherwise, and to believe their propaganda would be a fool's task.\nI'll leave it to you to decide whether or not you're a fool.","rew":"Experience: 550\n+10 reputation with Darnassus","done":"Yes ‹class›, thank you for coming. I apologize about the misunderstanding... the air is thick with mistrust between the Arch Druid here and Keeper Remulos in Moonglade. Each suspect the other of chicanery, and the fact that strange corruptions of Teldrassil continue unabated are still an issue here. It does little to quell mistrust.\nRegardless, our duty to the Cenarion Circle remains... even if those who lead it may disagree with one another.","pins":[{"z":"Darnassus","x":34.8,"y":9.3,"n":"Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":35.4,"y":8.4,"n":"Mathrengyl Bearwalker","e":1}],"cats":["darnassus"]},"7801":{"id":7801,"t":"Additional Runecloth","lv":60,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"20 Runecloth Stormwind Royal Guard , Honor Guard , Skullsplitter Speaker in Zul'Gurub , General Marcus Jonathan 85.7 % and 4 more","back":"Greetings once again, ‹name›! Our need for runecloth is constant, and we can always use additional resources if you are willing to part with them. For an additional stack of twenty runecloth, I will make sure that you are recognized for your continuing efforts on behalf of Darnassus.\nWhenever you are ready to hand in the stack of runecloth, I'll accept it.","done":"‹name› - without heroes like you working on behalf of Darnassus, we'd surely suffer. Thank you for your continued efforts!","pins":[{"z":"Darnassus","x":64,"y":23,"n":"Raedon Duskstriker","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darnassus"]},"1481":{"id":1481,"t":"The Corrupter","lv":33,"min":25,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring a Shadowstalker Scalp to Maurin Bonesplitter in Desolace.\nShadowstalker Scalp Hatefury Shadowstalker 33 %","desc":"I believe I can find this demon lord given the proper reagents.\nIf he is indeed as powerful as I suspect, I will need items gathered from deadly creatures. But you act in the Warchief's name, so I am sure you will accept my task.\nFirst, I will have to break any wards he has against scrying. For this, I will need the scalp from a satyr--but not any satyr. The scalp must come from a Hatefury shadowstalker.\nSearch for them among the ancient ruins in the northeast of Desolace.","rew":"Experience: 2,650\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"Do not bring me an incorrect scalp, ‹class›. Using the incorrect reagents could cause our deaths. The demon lord may have contingency spells on his person to slay those who would scry upon him.\nFate has already dealt me enough pain.","done":"The shadowstalkers were unable to slay you, ‹class›. Impressive... most impressive.\nThis scalp will do nicely for my spell. While you were away, I was able to gather some of the other reagents needed for the spell.\nI am almost ready. I only need a focus for the spell--something to project an image of the demon lord and his whereabouts.","pins":[{"z":"Desolace","x":52.2,"y":53.4,"n":"Maurin Bonesplitter","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["desolace"]},"5561":{"id":5561,"t":"Kodo Roundup","lv":34,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring five Tamed Kodos and the Kodo Kombobulator back to Smeed Scrabblescrew at Scrabblescrew's Camp.\nKodo Kombobulator\nKodos Tamed : 0/ 5\nProvided: Kodo Kombobulator","desc":"Bibbly thinks he is the only goblin in Desolace who knows how to make money. Well, the only caravan brave enough to travel these parts relies on me. Ever since I learned how to rejuvenate and control aged and dying kodos with my kodo kombobulator, the caravan owner Cork, Rigger, and I entered a partnership.\nTake the kombobulator and use it on any ancient, aged, or dying kodos; it will jolt the beast into a tamed kodo and force it to follow you. Once you have a kodo tamed, bring it back to me.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nKodo Rustler Boots Wrangling Spaulders\nExperience: 2,000\n+75 reputation with Ratchet","back":"The caravan will be here shortly; do you have the five new tamed kodos I was asking for?","done":"<Smeed Scrabblescrew begins counting.>\nThree, four, and five... excellent, I ask for five tamed kodos and I get five tamed kodos... I am going to be rich... yes, very rich! I hope to see the look on Bibbly's green face when he hears about my success!","pins":[{"z":"Desolace","x":60.9,"y":61.9,"n":"Smeed Scrabblescrew","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["desolace"]},"7481":{"id":7481,"t":"Elven Legends","lv":60,"min":54,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 8,300 experience instead of 8,550, 0.97 times as much.","obj":"Search Dire Maul for Kariel Winthalus. Report back to Sage Korolusk at Camp Mojache with whatever information that you may find.","desc":"Several years ago, a lone elven master named Kariel Winthalus fled the devastation of his homeland with several ancient elven artifacts in tow.\nOur search for this lost master lead us from the ruins of Quel'Thalas, through the Burning Steppes, across the great expanses of the sea, to Feralas.\nWe suspect that the elf sought sanctuary in the halls of Eldre'Thalas (what is now known as Dire Maul).\nYou must find him, adventurer. Whether alive or dead, the knowledge he carried must be recovered!","rew":"Money: 1 80 1 gold, 80 silver, 0 copper Experience: 8,300","back":"My associate, the night elf scholar, Runethorn, is recruiting her allies for this task.","done":"A shame... a tragedy. The items are lost you say? No trace of him, eh?","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":75.2,"y":43.8,"n":"Sage Korolusk","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["dire-maul"]},"6121":{"id":6121,"t":"Lessons Anew","lv":14,"min":14,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Moonglade and speak with Dendrite Starblaze in the village of Nighthaven.","desc":"You're now ready to learn about poison and the power we as druids have over it, ‹name›. Cenarius has blessed us with the ability to purge even the most foul of poisons with but a mere incantation. This gift is not to be taken lightly... and to ensure you learn this lesson, you'll work to address the effects of poisonings as a layman would.\nTravel to Moonglade and speak with Dendrite Starblaze; he awaits your arrival to begin your lesson.","rew":"Experience: 100\n+10 reputation with Cenarion Circle","done":"Greetings young ‹class›, I'm glad to see you ready and eager to learn about the curing of poisons.\nWhile most druids in the past were put through pre-planned trials, your work will involve no such thing. There has been a rash of animal poisonings in Auberdine, and the village there has been unable to cure it. To that end, a representative there has asked Moonglade for aid and we are sending you there to aid them. This is no exercise - the work you'll do is quite real. Bear this in mind.\nAlterac Mountains Darnassus Moonglade","pins":[{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":11.8,"y":56.6,"n":"Alfina Nightgaze","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":35.2,"y":8,"n":"Mathrengyl Bearwalker","s":1},{"z":"Moonglade","x":56.2,"y":30.4,"n":"Dendrite Starblaze","e":1}],"cats":["druid"]},"99161":{"id":99161,"t":"Rimes wrath","lv":8,"min":5,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Kill Avala and retrieve its core.\nAvala's Core","desc":"I noticed that the first elemental that appeared after the rockslide was larger than its peers. And from what I can tell, it has been the source of occasionally weather changes and other minor slides.\nI've been calling it 'Avala', if you could kill it and retrieve the core as proof, I will reward you.","rew":"You will receive:\nAvala's Binding\nExperience: 700","back":"'Ware the winter, friend.","done":"Light bless you, ‹class›. Your efforts make this area much safer and hopefully will prevent unnecessary deaths.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":57.6,"y":44.8,"n":"Father Gavin","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["dun-morogh"]},"1321":{"id":1321,"t":"The Black Shield","lv":35,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Show the Blackened Iron Shield to Do'gol in Brackenwall Village.\nBlackened Iron Shield\nProvided: Blackened Iron Shield","desc":"Hmm... I don't see anything out of the ordinary with this shield. We should have Do'gol, the blacksmith, take a look at it, and see if he can tell us more about it, but I wouldn't hold out hope...","rew":"Experience: 280","back":"Something for me, ‹class›?","done":"This is good shield. Very strong, heavy, good. But Do'gol don't need it. I make shields, not buy them, ‹name›.\nYou should know that.","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":36.4,"y":31.9,"n":"Krog","s":1},{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":36.5,"y":30.8,"n":"Do'gol","e":1}],"cats":["dustwallow-marsh"]},"6601":{"id":6601,"t":"Ascension...","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 4,950 experience instead of 5,450, 0.91 times as much.","obj":"It would appear as if the charade is over. You know that the Amulet of Draconic Subversion that Myranda the Hag created for you will not function inside Blackrock Spire. Perhaps you should find Rexxar and explain your predicament. Show him the Dull Drakefire Amulet. Hopefully he will know what to do next.\nDull Drakefire Amulet\nProvided: Dull Drakefire Amulet","desc":"From the skulls of our enemies is shaped a medallion. You know this medallion, yesss? You have no doubt seen it worn by your elders.\nTake it, whelp. Return to the Spire and present it to General Drakkisath. The General will place the final enchantment upon the medallion, attuning the trinket to your spirit.\nYou will wear the finished medallion as a badge of honor, symbolizing your ascension to one of our most guarded ranks: Guardian to the brood mother.\nGo!","rew":"Experience: 4,950","back":"Do not panic, ‹name›!","done":"It is merely dragon-talk, ‹name› - more hot air than actual substantive information. Pompous, aggressive behavior is to be expected from their kind.\nDustwallow Marsh Feralas","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":56.7,"y":87.7,"n":"Emberstrife","s":1},{"z":"Feralas","x":46.4,"y":18.2,"n":"Rexxar","e":1}],"cats":["dustwallow-marsh"]},"5241":{"id":5241,"t":"Uncle Carlin","lv":56,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Carlin Redpath.","desc":"Sometimes, when it's nighttime, I can hear my Uncle Carlin crying. It sounds like he's far away, to the east.\nI hope he's not crying for me! ‹name›, will you find my uncle and tell him I'm alright?\nIf you find him say I'm waiting for him, and I want to hear the story he used to tell... the one about the rabbits and the berry jam! That story's so funny!","rew":"Experience: 2,900","done":"You've seen Pamela? She's alive?\nShe's dead? No! Oh, Pamela! Why does your spirit still suffer in this world. Why are you perished, while fortune keeps me alive? In an instant I would switch places with you and wander dead Darrowshire, a ghost and alone!\nAh, but this news cannot change fate. Thank you, ‹name›. Now my duty, my duty to revenge, burns hot as ever.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":31.2,"y":78,"n":"Pamela Redpath","s":1},{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.7,"y":50,"n":"Carlin Redpath","e":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"6041":{"id":6041,"t":"When Smokey Sings, I Get Violent","lv":58,"min":54,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Plaguewood, northwest of Light's Hope. Destroy 8 Scourge Structures by using Smokey's Special Compound at the Mark of Detonation planted inside each building. Smokey has had the Ziggurats and Slaughterhouses marked.\nOnce you plant the bomb, leave the building and marvel at your handiwork.\nBy the way, Smokey's Special Compound is rather... unstable.\nScourge Structures Destroyed : 0/ 8\nProvided: Smokey's Special Compound","desc":"While you were gathering the supplies, I had some of my people handle marking the Scourge buildings we need demolished.\nHere's the plan: I'm going to give you ten sticks of my special compound. You're going to take them over to Plaguewood and plant them inside the Scourge structures that I've had marked for detonation.\n<Smokey snaps his fingers.>\nBing! It's just that easy.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nSmokey's Explosive Launcher Smokey's Fireshooter\nYou will also receive:\n10 Moist Towelette Smokey's Drape\nMoney: 2 65 2 gold, 65 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,200","back":"I got supplies left over to make a few more sticks of the special compound. Just let ol' Smokey know if you need more.","done":"You're much darker than I remember. You got that look going for you; the look that says, 'I've been charred by a high explosive bomb.'\n<Smokey laughs.>\nAnyhow! Here's your cut of the loot. I've thrown in a little something extra to help soothe the burns.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":70.9,"y":48.4,"n":"Smokey LaRue","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"5721":{"id":5721,"t":"The Battle of Darrowshire","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Place the Relic Bundle at the Darrowshire town square.\nPrevent Davil Lightfire's death until the death of Horgus.\nPrevent Captain Redpath's death until Redpath the Corrupted appears.\nDefeat Redpath the Corrupted.\nSpeak with the spirit of Joseph Redpath when he appears at the town square, then speak with Pamela at her home.\nAccept Redpath's Forgiveness\nProvided: Relic Bundle","desc":"Now, ‹name›, you will take part in battle of Darrowshire, and you will save Joseph Redpath.\nPlace this relic bundle in the Darrowshire town square, and the spirits of Darrowshire will rise. Join their battle and assure that these two things come to pass: Davil must survive beyond the death of Horgus, and Redpath must survive to be corrupted, then defeated.\nAfter defeating the corrupted Redpath, his spirit will be saved. Speak with him, then return to his daughter Pamela.","rew":"You will receive:\nTea with Sugar\nExperience: 8,300","back":"I think I heard ghosts outside. They whisper scary things to me...","done":"The fighting is over! I heard my daddy whisper to me. He scared away all the ghosts and he says he's coming home! I'm so happy!\nHe also said I should welcome you if came to our house, so I made some tea!\nI hope you like lots of sugar!\nWestern Plaguelands Eastern Plaguelands","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":39.5,"y":66.8,"n":"Chromie","s":1},{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":31.2,"y":78,"n":"Pamela Redpath","e":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"7961":{"id":7961,"t":"Waskily wabbits","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Kill 5 rabbits and return to Jon LeCraft by the forge on Designer Island.\nPolymorph Clone slain : 0/ 60\nThe Good Rabbit slain : 0/ 60\nZap a Polymorphed Chicken","desc":"These rabbits are breeding uncontrollably. Something must be done!\nHelp us ‹name›, you're our only hope.","rew":"You will receive:\n5 Rabbit's Foot Rabbit Crate (Snowshoe)\nMoney: 4 0 gold, 0 silver, 4 copper Experience: 20\n+25 reputation with Stormwind\nAzshara Open the zone on the world map Level 1 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 4 6 Side Both factions Shareable Yes Quest ID 7961","cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"3641":{"id":3641,"t":"Show Your Work","lv":47,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 6 Mithril Tubes, an Accurate Scope, and 2 Advanced Target Dummies to Tinkmaster Overspark in Ironforge.\n6 Mithril Tube\nAccurate Scope\n2 Advanced Target Dummy","desc":"As your mentor, I want some samples of your work. You're a skilled engineer; there is no question of this, ‹name›. What I hope to do though is to analyze your work for ways to emphasize gnome-oriented techniques in your future efforts. I need the following samples: six mithril tubes, an accurate scope, and two advanced target dummies.\nSubmit these items to me and I will issue you your own Gnome Engineer Membership Card; it is required for access to all gnome engineering trainers!","rew":"You will receive:\nGnome Engineer Membership Card\nYou will learn: Gnomish Engineer\nExperience: 3,150\n+75 reputation with Engineering - Gnome","back":"Once I receive your crafted engineering items for my review, I will hand you a genuine Gnome Engineer Membership Card! So long as the card is valid, you will have unlimited access to any gnome engineer trainer anywhere in the world.","done":"Here is your first Gnome Engineer Membership Card!\nThis card has its dues paid for in advance for fourteen days; all cards expire after two weeks of activity. When it does, pay your next set of dues to any gnome engineer trainer in order to get another card; without the card, your membership will temporarily lapse and you cannot access new schemata.\nThis never affects what you already know; once a gnome engineer, always a gnome engineer.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.2,"y":29.2,"n":"Tinkmaster Overspark","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["engineering"]},"4441":{"id":4441,"t":"Felbound Ancients","lv":54,"min":49,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Darnassus and use Eridan's Vial to collect a Vial of Blessed Water from the Temple of the Moon. Return to Eridan with the filled vial.\nVial of Blessed Water\nProvided: Eridan's Vial","desc":"The flute you found was carved from an ancient protector, the treant allies that have faithfully protected the night elves.\nThe satyrs have been able to corrupt anything they come in contact with, which includes the ancients that made Felwood their home. By the use of the fel, the spirit of the ancient has been bound and tortured, never completely released. The felbind you found is no doubt related.\nWe must try to purify the flute, ‹name›. Bring me blessed water from the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus.","rew":"Experience: 5,450","back":"The water will hopefully release the spirit of the ancient, and allow it to be at peace.","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. Now, we must pray that we can undo the damage that has been done...\nFelwood Darnassus","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":51.3,"y":81.5,"n":"Eridan Bluewind","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"4521":{"id":4521,"t":"Wild Guardians","lv":56,"min":52,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Trull Failbane in Felwood wants you to kill 15 Raging Owlbeasts and 15 Ragged Owlbeasts.\nRaging Owlbeast slain : 0/ 15\nRagged Owlbeast slain : 0/ 15","desc":"Winterspring lies just beyond Timbermaw, northeast of Felwood. Have you been there?\nI have heard that the area is laden with creatures called wildkin. These beasts have been known to guard secrets; secrets of the Night elves.\nWe must figure out what may be hidden in Winterspring.\nI have heard the ragged owlbeasts can be found just south of the road, and that there are others called raging owlbeasts that may be found in the center of Winterspring. Clear them out, and gain access to the land.","rew":"Money: 85 0 gold, 85 silver, 0 copper Experience: 5,800\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Report back to me after you have completed the task I gave you.","done":"This is excellent news, ‹name›. With these beasts out of the way, we can begin to adventure further into Winterspring. Are you ready for more?\nFelwood Winterspring","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":34.7,"y":52.8,"n":"Trull Failbane","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"4281":{"id":4281,"t":"Thalanaar Delivery","lv":44,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Undelivered Parcel to Falfindel Waywarder in Thalanaar.\nUndelivered Parcel\nProvided: Undelivered Parcel","desc":"This parcel of goods you found in the Woodpaw gnoll camps was supposed to be delivered to the small way-station of Thalanaar in southeastern Feralas. Regardless of the missing courier's fate, the task of delivering the parcel remains unfinished.\nExamining the parcel in detail reveals a hand written name of \"Falfindel Waywarder\" on the outside of the packaging. Perhaps this is the parcel's ultimate recipient.","rew":"Money: 65 0 gold, 65 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,800\n+75 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Welcome to Thalanaar, ‹class›. Do you need assistance of some sort?","done":"Elune be praised, the delivery from Feathermoon Stronghold has finally arrived!\nYour presence here indicates to me that perhaps some ill fate may have befallen Raschal, our usual courier. I hope that everything works out. I know that recently, the Woodpaw have become highly agitated from some source to their south. Maybe he fell to the wilds there; I would be careful, friend.\nRegardless, thank you again. Here is payment for this parcel's delivery.","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":89.6,"y":46.6,"n":"Falfindel Waywarder","e":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"7721":{"id":7721,"t":"Fuel for the Zapping","lv":48,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Collect 10 Water Elemental Cores from the Sea Elementals and Sea Sprays along the Forgotten Coast of Feralas, and bring them back to Zorbin Fandazzle who is near the dock there.\n10 Water Elemental Core Sea Elemental 50 % , Sea Spray 50 %","desc":"If I bet against my own better judgment and stay to run an engineering shop along the Forgotten Coast, I will need to deal with these pesky elementals. Curse the powers of elementalism unchecked, I say!\nFortunately for me, and now for you my hopeful agent provocateur, the elementals represent an ideal source of raw power for my Ultra-Shrinker refinement - give them the what-for I say! When doing this though, be sure to save me the water elemental cores!","rew":"You will receive:\nZorbin's Water Resistant Hat\nMoney: 70 0 gold, 70 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,400\n+150 reputation with Steamwheedle Cartel","back":"While I could bore you with the technical details of the utility behind elemental cores, I will instead tempt you to completion of this important task by offering valuable coin and prizes for doing so. Yon verily, are you finished?","done":"Scrumdillyriffic! These cores will keep me working for some time. Add to that the benefit of there now being fewer elementals along the coast, and I might no longer cry myself to sleep at the prospect of having set up shop in perhaps the worst place imaginable!\nThank you, ‹name›, for your efforts on my behalf. While it certainly straps me financially to do this, allow me to show you some gratitude you may understand and appreciate... loot!","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":44.8,"y":43.4,"n":"Zorbin Fandazzle","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"4041":{"id":4041,"t":"The Videre Elixir","lv":52,"min":47,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Evoroot Evoroot","rew":"You will receive:\n3 Videre Elixir","back":"Bring me an Evoroot, and sure, I can make ya that Videre Elixir.\nI know all kinds of things about herbs and alchemy... Why, let me tell you the story about the time I transmuted gold from the cheese I was going to eat for lunch... hey... Where are you going?","done":"So, you pulled a fast one on ol' Miblon, eh?","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":45.1,"y":25.6,"n":"Gregan Brewspewer","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"4601":{"id":4601,"t":"The Sparklematic 5200!","lv":30,"min":25,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays -1g -3s instead of 0.","obj":"Insert a Grime-Encrusted Item into the Sparklematic 5200, and be sure to have three silver coins to start the machine.\nGrime-Encrusted Object Holdout Technician 25 % , Holdout Medic 25 % , Holdout Warrior 25 % , Irradiated Pillager 25 % and 4 more","desc":"This contraption stands out amongst the gnomes holding out against the madness outside the room. A small plaque on the device reads \"The Sparklematic 5200\", followed by some text:\n\"Grime and residue ruining your sparklies? The Sparklematic 5200 puts the shine back in shine-tastic! Insert the item you wish to clean and deposit three silver coins in the coin slot. Give the Sparklematic 5200 a moment for operation, and voila! Your valuables will emerge clean and shiny!\"","back":"It would seem that the device needs some sort of grime-encrusted object to clean and three silver coins to get the contraption working. So long as both are present, the Sparklematic 5200 should work...","done":"You insert the grime-encrusted item and three silver coins into the Sparklematic 5200. The machine surges to live in an almost frenzied attempt to purge the grime from the unknown item. Loud, violent churning sounds beat from the heart of the machine. The metal frame of the beast creaks and groans as it lurches from side to side...\nStart The Sparklematic 5200 End The Sparklematic 5200 Level 30 , requires level 25 Difficulty 25 26 28 33 38 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Type Dungeon Shareable Yes Quest ID 4601\nThe chain\n3 quests at level 30, 2,450 XP in all.\n1 [ 30 ] The Sparklematic 5200! this quest\nInsert a Grime-Encrusted Item into the Sparklematic 5200, and be sure to have three silver coins to start the machine.\nThe Sparklematic 5200\n2 [ 30 ] The Sparklematic 5200!\nThe Sparklematic 5200\n2,450 XP\n3 [ 30 ] More Sparklematic Action\nThe Sparklematic 5200","cats":["gnomeregan"]},"2841":{"id":2841,"t":"Rig Wars","lv":35,"min":25,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 6,550 experience instead of 2,750, 2.38 times as much. Read from what the game server sent.","obj":"Retrieve the Rig Blueprints and Thermaplugg's Safe Combination from Gnomeregan and bring them to Nogg in Orgrimmar.\nRig Blueprints Thermaplugg's Safe\nThermaplugg's Safe Combination Mekgineer Thermaplugg","desc":"Gnome technology - two years ago its most common use was as a punch line. Times certainly have changed. Now they've got a new rig built that's better than all our shredder models combined. I need the blueprints, ‹name›!\nUnfortunately, the plans are locked away in a safe near Mekgineer Thermaplugg. To make matters worse, the combination to the safe is only known by Mekgineer Thermaplugg.\nDo whatever you have to do to get that combination, ‹name›. Then crack open that safe and bring back those blueprints!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nCivinad Robes Triprunner Dungarees Dual Reinforced Leggings\nExperience: 6,550\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"I don't see any blueprints. Did you hide them somewhere on your body or are you just standing around here to irritate me?","done":"I knew you could do it, ‹name›! Sovik on the other hand, he had his doubts.\n<Nogg clears his throat.>\nNow that we have the blueprints in our possession, it is only a matter of time before we figure out all of the gnomish innovations that went into the creation of the rig and make them goblin innovations for our new shredder models.\nOrgrimmar Dun Morogh","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":76,"y":25.4,"n":"Nogg","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["gnomeregan"]},"521":{"id":521,"t":"The Crown of Will","lv":43,"min":34,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver the Crown of Will to Sharlindra in the Undercity.\nCrown of Will Mug'thol\nProvided: Crown of Will","desc":"All that remains is to deliver the Crown of Will to Sharlindra in the Undercity. She will see that it is delivered to Lady Sylvanas. I would warn you against thinking to use it for your own purposes, ‹name›, Mug'Thol's fate should be illustration enough.","rew":"You will receive:\nEthereal Talisman\nExperience: 3,600\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"I note that your task is unfinished, ‹name›. Shall I inform Sharlindra of your ineptitude?","done":"So this is the relic the ogre used to duck the will of the Dark Lady...\nStrange that something so simple could wield so great a power. And to fall into as clumsy hands as those. Well done, ‹name›, I will deliver the crown to Lady Sylvanas, and see that she hears of your accomplishment.\nHillsbrad Foothills Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":62.6,"y":20.6,"n":"Melisara","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":57.6,"y":93.8,"n":"Sharlindra","e":1}],"cats":["hillsbrad-foothills"]},"2041":{"id":2041,"t":"Speak with Shoni","lv":15,"min":15,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Shoni the Shilent in Stormwind.","desc":"Perhaps... Perhaps you can help us in the battle for Gnomeregan.\nIn Stormwind you will find the commander of our underground assault crew, Shoni the Shilent. Shoni needs assistance with her gyrodrillmatic excavationators.\nYou will probably find her amongst the dwarves in Stormwind.\nGood luck, ‹name›.","rew":"Experience: 270\n+25 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","done":"Do you bring word from central command?\nDun Morogh Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.2,"y":29.2,"n":"Gnoarn","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":62.6,"y":34.1,"n":"Shoni the Shilent","e":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"9001":{"id":9001,"t":"Saving the Best for Last","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Give Deliana your Magister's Crown and Magister's Robes.\nMagister's Crown Darkmaster Gandling 0 %\nMagister's Robes General Drakkisath 0 %","desc":"That's an amazing story, ‹name›! You have my thanks, and the heartfelt gratitude of all who were involved. Now maybe I'll be able to sleep at night with both eyes shut.\nAs to your reward, I believe I have a few things that you'll really enjoy.","rew":"You will receive:\nSorcerer's Crown Sorcerer's Robes\nExperience: 1,650","back":"As per our deal, are you ready to hand over your Magister's pieces in exchange for your new Sorcerer's Crown and Robes?","done":"I'm going to miss you, ‹name›. I owe you such a debt of gratitude; I think I'll never be able to repay it.\nI hope that you enjoy your new head and chest armor, and that it protects you for a long time to come.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":58.1,"y":29.5,"n":"Deliana","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"8681":{"id":8681,"t":"Thunderhorn the Elder","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin of Ancestry\n+50 reputation with Horde\n+50 reputation with Alliance","done":"Your spirit burns with life, young ‹class›. I accept the homage you pay, and offer in return this token...","pins":[{"z":"Un'Goro Crater","x":50.4,"y":76.1,"n":"Elder Thunderhorn","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["lunar-festival"]},"1881":{"id":1881,"t":"Speak with Anastasia","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Anastasia Hartwell.","desc":"‹name›, Anastasia Hartwell has a task for someone of your talents. Speak with her in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity, and prepare yourself for your first task for the mages of the Forsaken.","rew":"Experience: 85","done":"Greetings, ‹name›. You were wise to answer my call, and wiser still if you heed what I next say...\nTirisfal Glades Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":62,"y":52.5,"n":"Cain Firesong","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":85.1,"y":10,"n":"Anastasia Hartwell","e":1}],"cats":["mage"]},"1961":{"id":1961,"t":"Gathering Materials","lv":15,"min":15,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 10 Linen Cloth and 6 Dalaran Mana Gems to Josef Gregorian.\n10 Linen Cloth Kogan Forgestone , Lisan Pierce , Adam Lind 66.7 % , Hidden Strongbox 58.6 % and 4 more\n6 Dalaran Mana Gem Dalaran Miner 80 % , Dalaran Brewmaster 80 % , Dalaran Conjuror 80 % , Dalaran Mage 80 % and 4 more","desc":"It is time for you to don your first mage's robes, ‹name›. They are a sign of your station, and a testament to your worth.\nTo gain the robes, you must gather the mana gems from the Dalaran mages of Silverpine. Their beliefs are similar to ours and so killing them is somewhat distasteful, but if they lack the strength to resist us, then they do not deserve their lives.\nBring the gems and a supply of linen to Josef Gregorian at the Magic Quarter's tailor shop.","rew":"Experience: 800","back":"Anastasia said you would come to me, and I am prepared to fashion your robes. Do you have the gems and the linen?","done":"This is very good material, and although I lack the talent to gauge the quality of these mana gems, we'll soon know if they possess the power needed to create spellfire robes...\nUndercity Silverpine Forest","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":85.1,"y":10,"n":"Anastasia Hartwell","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":70.8,"y":30.7,"n":"Josef Gregorian","e":1}],"cats":["mage"]},"761":{"id":761,"t":"Swoop Hunting","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 8 Trophy Swoop Quills to Harken Windtotem in Bloodhoof Village.\n8 Trophy Swoop Quill Wiry Swoop 70 % , Swoop 70 % , Taloned Swoop 70 %","desc":"The swoop is a cunning bird, and difficult to find and hunt. A collection of Swoop Quills is a badge of cleverness and determination for a hunter.\nIf you are willing to take up this task, then enter the plains and hunt the swoop.\nBring me their quills, and bring honor to your clan.\nThe swoops may be found anywhere in Mulgore, but your eyes must be sharp to spot them, and your hooves must be quick to catch them.","rew":"Money: 2 50 0 gold, 2 silver, 50 copper Experience: 675\n+150 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"Have you found the swoops, ‹name›. Do you have their quills?","done":"I know that gathering these quills was not an easy task, ‹name›. In doing this, you prove that you are a ‹class› of merit. It is good to have you at Bloodhoof Village.","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":47.7,"y":62.7,"n":"Harken Windtotem","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["mulgore"]},"99081":{"id":99081,"t":"Grim tidings","lv":9,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring Longwalker Malah's Report to Brave Wildrunner in Bloodhoof Village.\nLongwalker Malah's Report","desc":"You can see what appears to be a new centaur camp in the direction the arrows in Malah's back would have come from. There is a stir of activity, suggesting a small raiding party has made its way into Mulgore.\nThe Longwalker has a report in her still-clenched hand. Brave Wildrunner will want to know of Malah's fate--and her killers.","done":"This is most dire news indeed. We must inform Baine at once!","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":57.6,"y":63.2,"n":"Malah Longwind","s":1},{"z":"Mulgore","x":46.6,"y":63,"n":"Brave Wildrunner","e":1}],"cats":["mulgore"]},"9081":{"id":9081,"t":"Bonescythe Sabatons","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays -25g instead of 0.","obj":"Rohan the Assassin at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make Bonescythe Sabatons if you bring him the following: 1 Desecrated Sabatons, 12 Wartorn Leather Scraps, 3 Cured Rugged Hides, 2 Nexus Crystals and 25 gold pieces.\nDesecrated Sabatons Gluth 0 % in Naxxramas , Gothik the Harvester 0 % in Naxxramas , Instructor Razuvious 0 % in Naxxramas\n12 Wartorn Leather Scrap Skeletal Steed 26.1 % in Naxxramas , Necro Knight Guardian 26.1 % in Naxxramas , Infectious Ghoul 24.5 % in Naxxramas , Stoneskin Gargoyle 24.1 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\n3 Cured Rugged Hide\n2 Nexus Crystal","desc":"If you want Bonescythe made, you're going to have to supply the materials.\nEnter Naxxramas, the big floating city of death in the sky up there, and find desecrated armor and wartorn armor scraps. Bring those back along with the materials to put everything together and you'll have your Bonescythe. Oh, and you'll need to pay me for my troubles... I'll supply the bones.","rew":"You will receive:\nBonescythe Sabatons\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Just bring me the materials and stop wasting my time, ‹class›.","done":"They go on your feet. Say, you haven't been nosing around in Tyr's Hand again, have you?","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.6,"y":48.9,"n":"Rohan the Assassin","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"9241":{"id":9241,"t":"Polar Bracers","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays -200g instead of 0.","obj":"Craftsman Wilhelm at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands wants 4 Frozen Runes, 12 Enchanted Leather, 3 Essence of Water, 3 Cured Rugged Hides and 200 gold.\n4 Frozen Rune Frozen Rune in Naxxramas\n12 Enchanted Leather sold by Lhara\n3 Essence of Water Princess Tempestria 70.6 % , Lord Skwol 53.3 % , Hydrospawn 11 % , Toxic Horror 7.2 % and 4 more\n3 Cured Rugged Hide","desc":"Thanks to you and Omarion (May he rest in peace), I am now able to create Polar bracers. All you need to do is bring me the materials and pay a small crafting fee.","rew":"You will receive:\nPolar Bracers","back":"Have you brought the materials?","done":"Here is your order, ‹name›. Delivered as promised!","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.2,"y":49.9,"n":"Craftsman Wilhelm","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"98601":{"id":98601,"t":"A difficult path","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Read the Consecrated Scroll and speak to Aramis Hammerhand in the church in Deathknell.\nProvided: Consecrated Scroll","desc":"While you were off dealing with the mindless Scourge, this scroll arrived for you. It reeks of the light, so I imagine its of some importance to a paladin like yourself.\nRead it before heading out again. Just please--step away when you do. Paladins make me quite uneasy.","back":"Through pain comes resolve.","done":"Your training can now begin in earnest, ‹class›. I see great promise in you, but take care not to turn away from the light, even for a moment. Embrace the pain it will cause you. That pain is a crucible, and you will emerge from it stronger than you ever were in your previous life.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":30.8,"y":66.2,"n":"Shadow Priest Sarvis","s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":31,"y":66.2,"n":"Aramis Hammerhand","e":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"94441":{"id":94441,"t":"A lesson in divinity","lv":12,"min":12,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Danitha Morr in the keep at Bandarion Keep.","desc":"Please give my thanks to Danitha Morr and tell her that the rest of the Deathguard will hear about the service that the paladins of Tyr's Watch performed for us.\nYou have a lot of promise as a paladin, and I am proud to have those like you among the ranks of the Forsaken. Dark Lady watch over you, ‹name›.","done":"The Symbol of Life is only able to be used by a ‹class› who is ready to make use of one of the light's greatest blessings. I'm proud to count you among us, and I now bestow upon you the gift of redemption. With this you will be able to resurrect your fallen companions. Use this new boon wisely.\nYou have done well for both the Forsaken as well as the paladins of Tyr's Watch. Any steps we can take to win the hearts and minds of our fellow Forsaken is well worth the effort. Go with the light, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":22,"y":44.6,"n":"Deathguard Billmuth","s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":22,"y":44.6,"n":"Danitha Morr","e":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"1641":{"id":1641,"t":"The Tome of Divinity","lv":12,"min":12,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nTome of Divinity","done":"Here in Stormwind, I am responsible for putting paladins on the path to greater virtue as they devote themselves to the Light and defend Azeroth from the Scourge and other threats.\nThe time has come for you to take your first step towards being truly virtuous. If you accept it, I will give you a Book of Divinity. In studying it, you shall learn some about the Light, and what is expected of you. If you understand it, and are capable, then you will succeed in attaining greater abilities.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":50.5,"y":47.5,"n":"Duthorian Rall","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"7641":{"id":7641,"t":"The Work of Grimand Elmore","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Grimand Elmore in Stormwind's Dwarven District.","desc":"A paladin's charger is nothing more than a pack animal without proper barding for it. The barding used by your charger not only needs to be of the finest materials possible, but because of the circumstances involved it must also be sufficiently attuned to the spirit realm.\nFirst things first, ‹name› - let's get your barding made. In Stormwind's Dwarven District is one of the finest craftsmen living today, Grimand Elmore. His work will not be cheap, but his quality is what we seek. Speak with him.","rew":"Experience: 650","done":"Hello there - Lord Shadowbreaker sent me word ahead of time that you'd be coming around this way to see me. I'm willing to make the barding you need, but it won't be either cheap or easy; let's get that out in the open first and foremost.\nI will say this much, and Grayson will back me up when I make this claim... you'll not find better barding made anywhere in all of Azeroth than right here.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":48.4,"y":50.2,"n":"Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":59.7,"y":33.8,"n":"Grimand Elmore","e":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"5641":{"id":5641,"t":"A Lack of Fear","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Renamed from A Lack of Fear.","obj":"Speak to High Priest Rohan in Ironforge.","desc":"‹name›, your High Priest Rohan would have an audience with you in Ironforge. Make haste, my strong friend, your next test quickly approaches. Although I wish I could bear witness to your race's own special rites, my place is here. But may the Light go with you in your travels. Rohan should still be in the Mystic Ward once you reach the city. He will be waiting.","rew":"You will learn: Fear Ward","done":"You've got the makings of a great ‹class›, ‹name›. Keep up the good work!\nYou've already shown you're ready for battle. Perhaps it's time we taught ya a little somethin' more.\nStormwind City Dun Morogh","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":49.5,"y":44.6,"n":"High Priestess Laurena","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":55,"y":22.4,"n":"High Priest Rohan","e":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"6521":{"id":6521,"t":"An Unholy Alliance","lv":36,"min":28,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 3,500 experience instead of 5,250, 0.67 times as much. New rewards: Cultist's Chestguard. Reported by players.","obj":"Bring Ambassador Malcin's Head to Varimathras in the Undercity.\nAmbassador Malcin's Head Ambassador Malcin","desc":"Malcin claims he is outside Razorfen Downs. This ambassador must be slain--his mission a failure in the eyes of the Lich King.\nHis presence there does explain much of what we've discovered about the area--some of the quilboar have grown frightfully powerful while showing signs of the Plague in their own way. Truly that must be a sign of some sort of deal they've struck.\nFind Malcin and slay him, ‹name›. Return to me after the deed is done.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nSkullbreaker Nail Spitter Zealot's Robe Cultist's Chestguard\nNew in Forever: Cultist's Chestguard.\nMoney: 20 0 gold, 20 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,500","back":"Have you found the Ambassador, ‹name›? Is he dead?\nWe cannot afford to allow the Scourge to take a foothold on Kalimdor. They are enough of a threat to our own borders to have to deal with them on two fronts.\nThe only optimistic sign from the events you've told me about is that the crone seemed uncorrupted. She must know deep in her spirit that the Scourge may bring great power, but that the Barrens would not truly be hers if she were to agree to their deal.","done":"Good. Well done, ‹class›.\nNow that Malcin is dead, we can at least know that the Scourges advances will be halted. The Dark Lady thanks you for your efforts and wishes to reward you with a gift.\nAlthough we do not know the extent of the Scourges influence within the Downs, I am sure we will discover their plots soon enough.","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":56.3,"y":92.2,"n":"Varimathras","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["razorfen-downs"]},"121":{"id":121,"t":"Messenger to Stormwind","lv":14,"min":14,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take General Marcus Jonathan's letter of response to Magistrate Solomon in Lakeshire.\nThe General's Response\nProvided: The General's Response","desc":"While I wait for a response from the King I want you to carry this letter to Magistrate Solomon.\nDismissed, ‹class›!","rew":"Money: 1 50 0 gold, 1 silver, 50 copper Experience: 250\n+25 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Did the General send news? Are reinforcements on the way?","done":"Thank you for your time, ‹class›. For your service to Lakeshire and Stormwind I reward you with these coins.\nNow if you'll excuse me, I find this correspondence somewhat of a mystery. Something is amiss in our Kingdom. I fear this is the beginning of conflict, not the end.\nStormwind City Redridge Mountains","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":69.2,"y":82.7,"n":"General Marcus Jonathan","s":1},{"z":"Redridge Mountains","x":24.9,"y":44.5,"n":"Magistrate Solomon","e":1}],"cats":["redridge-mountains"]},"8841":{"id":8841,"t":"Ten Commendation Signets","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"10 Horde Commendation Signet","back":"I accept commendation signets from adventurers who have received them in the line of duty. For each set of ten that you hand to me, I'll make sure that you receive a significant acknowledgement of your deeds with Orgrimmar. I also accept single tokens, but at a much reduced rate of recognition. We are much more interested in greater feats of duty, though no feat will be ignored.\nWith that said, I'll gladly take your signets if you are ready to hand in a set.","done":"Excellent! It is no small sacrifice that you've made to earn these signets, and you will be acknowledged for your service appropriately. It's adventurers like you, ‹name›, that truly make a difference.\nLet me know if you have additional signets to hand in; I'll gladly help you out with whatever ones you need exchanged.","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":61.9,"y":45.3,"n":"Officer Gothena","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["reputation"]},"95161":{"id":95161,"t":"Remember that i love you","lv":22,"min":15,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Deliver the Blood-Stained Letter to Avette Fellwood in Duskwood.\nProvided: Blood-Stained Letter","desc":"If you're looking for Jeremy Heartweaver, your best bet is to talk to his newly adopted mother, Avette Fellwood out in Duskwood. Sweet woman. Likely needs another pair of hands for her work, but it beats staying in the orphanage.\nIf you see little Jeremy do be sure to tell him we're all thinking of him, won't you?","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nTarnished Locket\nExperience: 180","back":"Yes? What do you need?","done":"Oh no...\nIt's nice of you to bring this, but I don't think Jeremy is ready to see it. Matron Nightingale said my little Jeremy hasn't spoken since the attack on Lordaeron, and I don't intend to force him now. Showing him this will only cause him more pain.\nDon't look at me like that. I won't hide his past from him, but he needs time to heal. I'll give this to him when he's older. Thank you for stopping by, but I think it's time you should go.\nStormwind City Duskwood","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":47.2,"y":38.4,"n":"Orphan Matron Nightingale","s":1},{"z":"Duskwood","x":73.2,"y":44.8,"n":"Avette Fellwood","e":1}],"cats":["riverglades"]},"2281":{"id":2281,"t":"Redridge Rendezvous","lv":16,"min":16,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Venture forth to Lakeshire in the Redridge Mountains and speak with Lucius.","desc":"Sending you out in the field now would be suicide. Renzik doesn't need another dead rogue on his hands. Don't fret, though, ‹name› - Renzik is going to get you up to speed.\nMake your way to the Redridge Mountains and speak with an associate of SI:7 named Lucius. You will find him hanging around the docks of Lakeshire with the other shady good-for-nothings.","rew":"Experience: 120","done":"Ah, so your fingers are a little fat, eh? Don't worry, ‹name›, I've turned more useless thieves than you into accomplished rogues.\nStormwind City Redridge Mountains","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":78.3,"y":71.1,"n":"Renzik \"The Shiv\"","s":1},{"z":"Redridge Mountains","x":23,"y":52,"n":"Lucius","e":1}],"cats":["rogue"]},"6681":{"id":6681,"t":"The Manor, Ravenholdt","lv":24,"min":24,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Seal of Ravenholdt to Fahrad at Ravenholdt Manor, hidden away in the hills of Hillsbrad.\nYour cunning will be tested along the way. Be prepared.\nSeal of Ravenholdt\nRite of Cunning\nProvided: Seal of Ravenholdt","desc":"‹name›,\nRavenholdt has taken an interest in you, young thief. We have been watching. Your style is a bit awkward but nothing we couldn't fix.\nShould you be prepared to embark on a career as a disciple of Master Ravenholdt and member of the Assassin's League, you have only to bring the Seal of Ravenholdt (attached to this letter) to Ravenholdt Manor.\nYour first task is to find the manor, hidden away in the hills of Hillsbrad and demonstrate your cunning.\nRegards,\nFahrad","rew":"Experience: 1,950\n+100 reputation with Ravenholdt","back":"Did you meet Milton?<Fahrad laughs.>","done":"Most excellent, young thief.\nYou look a bit beaten down, but no worse for the wear.\nA long journey awaits you - long and rewarding. Are you prepared to finally embrace your destiny among the masters of Ravenholdt?\nSpeak with the guards outside. They will get you started.\nAlterac Mountains Hillsbrad Foothills","pins":[{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":84.4,"y":80.3,"n":"Fahrad","e":1}],"cats":["rogue"]},"3481":{"id":3481,"t":"Trinkets...","lv":50,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Open the chest.","desc":"The chest appears locked.","rew":"You will receive:\nHoard of the Black Dragonflight\nExperience: 470","done":"The chest opens at your touch. How much cheese could possibly be in here? There is only one way to find out.","pins":[{"z":"Searing Gorge","x":38.8,"y":39,"n":"Hoard of the Black Dragonflight","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["searing-gorge"]},"92841":{"id":92841,"t":"Valley of bones","lv":40,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Improve your reputation with the Magram, and locate Orgrul near the Valley of Bones south of Magram Village.\nMagram Clan Centaur","desc":"It is time, outsider, for you to learn of our great discovery... but Warug will not be the one to tell it!\nHead south to the other end of the village. Look for a big, stinky centaur named Orgrul.\nYou will know when you get there.\nYou will know when you see him.\nIf he thinks you deserve to know, you will know.\nAnd if he doesn't? Well. You can be happy knowing Warug has a new crown.\nLevel 40 , requires level 35 Difficulty 35 36 38 43 51 Side Both factions Shareable Yes Quest ID 92841\nThe chain\n15 quests from level 32 to 43, 36,630 XP in all.\n1 [ 35 ] Brutal Politics\nGain a Friendly reputation with the Magram, then speak with Warug.\nCaptain Pentigast Desolace\n2,050 XP\n2 [ 32 ] Assault on the Kolkar\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram.\nWarug Desolace\n2,550 XP\n[ 33 ] Magram Alliance\nGain a Friendly reputation with the Magram, then speak with Warug.\nGurda Wildmane Desolace\n650 XP\n3 [ 33 ] Broken Tears\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram, and bring 3 Broken Tears to Warug in the Magram Village.\nWarug Desolace\n2,650 XP\n4 [ 40 ] A Conqueror's Crown\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram, and return a Conqueror's Crown from the Badlands to Warug in Magram Village.\n3,150 XP\n5 [ 40 ] Valley of Bones this quest\nImprove your reputation with the Magram, and locate Orgrul near the Valley of Bones south of Magram Village.\n320 XP\n6 [ 42 ] Mountain of Bones\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram, and bring 426 Gently Cursed Bones to Orgrul south of the Magram Village in Desolace.\n3,450 XP\n7 [ 42 ] Corrupting Tears\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram, and bring 3 Petrified Bark and 3 Imbued Tears back to Orgrul.\n3,450 XP\n8 [ 41 ] Proof of Concept\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram Clan, then bring 426 Well Cursed Bones from a successful ritual back to Orgrul.\n2,450 XP\n9 [ 40 ] Bone Raising\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram Clan, and use the Enhanced Necromancy Staff to fully raise undead that are struggling to emerge throughout the Valley of Bones.\n2,350 XP\n[ 42 ] No Mercy for the Weak\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram Clan, and slay 5 Gelkis Captives scattered around the Valley of Bones.\n2,550 XP\n10 [ 43 ] Bristleback Retreat\nMaintain your re","cats":["shendralas"]},"8281":{"id":8281,"t":"Stepping Up Security","lv":57,"min":54,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Windcaller Proudhorn at Cenarion Hold in Silithus wants you to slay 20 Dredge Crushers.\nDredge Crusher slain : 0/ 20","desc":"Your performance has been truly exemplary so far, ‹name›. Our supply lines are not completely safe yet, however. In the absence of dredge strikers, their larger southern cousins will surely move in to take their place in the north.\nYou'll have to kill quite a few dredge crushers to keep them at bay, but we cannot leave the safety of our supply lines to chance.","rew":"Money: 1 70 1 gold, 70 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,000\n+100 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"The dredge crushers are a serious threat and must be dealt with at once!","done":"Excellent! You've proven to be a valuable ally in preparing for the war against the silithid.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":51.2,"y":38.3,"n":"Windcaller Proudhorn","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"8361":{"id":8361,"t":"Abyssal Contacts","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bor Wildmane at Cenarion Hold in Silithus wants you to destroy an Abyssal Templar and bring him an Abyssal Crest as proof of the deed.\nAbyssal Crest Crimson Templar , Azure Templar , Hoary Templar , Earthen Templar","desc":"We've seen the Twilight's Hammer cultists performing rituals to summon powerful elemental nobles. We don't know if these are the beings the cultists worship or if they act as intermediaries to even more powerful forces. One thing is for sure: they are receiving orders from these elementals.\nI want you to find a way to contact an Abyssal Templar and give it a proper beating! Nothing throws the troops in disarray like taking out the chain of command. Bring back proof while you're at it.","rew":"You will receive:\nBag of Spoils\nMoney: 90 0 gold, 90 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"Did you finish the job?","done":"Hah! You did it, ‹name›! The Twilight's Hammer will soon be crushed!","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":48.6,"y":37.8,"n":"Bor Wildmane","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"441":{"id":441,"t":"Raleigh and the Undercity","lv":16,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Deliah's Ring to Raleigh.\nDeliah's Ring\nProvided: Deliah's Ring","desc":"Deliah had a husband, Raleigh, who now dwells in the Undercity. If the Deliah who lived in Brill is the one who owned this ring, then Raleigh will know.\nRaleigh is in the Trade Quarter of the Undercity.","rew":"Experience: 575\n+50 reputation with Undercity","back":"Do I know you?","done":"Yes, this ring was my wife's. Her fate was the fate of all who fail to endure these harsh times. I feel nothing for her death, nor for the story you tell of her body's abduction.\nSuch feelings have long since grown cold within me. But desire does still burn in my dead heart, ‹name›.\nDesire for revenge.\nTirisfal Glades Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":61.3,"y":50.8,"n":"Magistrate Sevren","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":62,"y":42.7,"n":"Raleigh Andrean","e":1}],"cats":["silverpine-forest"]},"5881":{"id":5881,"t":"Calling in the Reserves","lv":28,"min":23,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Maggran wishes you to deliver a letter to Grish Longrunner at the Great Lift in the Barrens.\nMaggran's Reserve Letter\nProvided: Maggran's Reserve Letter","desc":"The Horde does well keeping our troops fresh... since the Great War we have been prosperous here in Kalimdor.\nI need you to do me a favor, I have a lad by the name of Grish Longrunner protecting the Great Lift in the southern barrens. Give him this letter; the letter will let him know that I have a reserve warrior coming to relieve him of duty so that he can visit his family. He requested this sometime ago and he would be happy to hear the news.","rew":"Money: 12 0 gold, 12 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,150\n+50 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"You have news from Maggran Earthbinder?","done":"This is great news; I have been sitting here guarding this hunk of wood for too long. Now I can spend some time with my family... Yippee!\nStonetalon Mountains Thousand Needles","pins":[{"z":"Stonetalon Mountains","x":47.2,"y":61.2,"n":"Maggran Earthbinder","s":1},{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":31.9,"y":21.7,"n":"Grish Longrunner","e":1}],"cats":["stonetalon-mountains"]},"1081":{"id":1081,"t":"Reception from Tyrande","lv":28,"min":17,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Tyrande Whisperwind in Darnassus.","desc":"‹name›, I am sure Tyrande Whisperwind herself would like to thank you for taking part in this mission.\nIt may not appear so on the surface, but what you've helped start could very well strengthen our foothold in the Stonetalon Mountains.\nIf you consider yourself our ally against these atrocities, go see Tyrande in the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nEfflorescent Robe Grizzly Tunic Wildwood Chain\nYou will also receive:\nBand of Elven Grace\nExperience: 3,400\n+200 reputation with Alliance","done":"Hello, ‹name›. I have indeed heard your name before, and although you are still full of youth, I am pleased to see the path you have set for yourself.\nYou would do me a great honor if you would accept this as a gift of appreciation.\nAshenvale Darnassus","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":34.9,"y":49.8,"n":"Sentinel Thenysil","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":39.1,"y":81.6,"n":"Tyrande Whisperwind","e":1}],"cats":["stonetalon-mountains"]},"1241":{"id":1241,"t":"The Missing Diplomat","lv":28,"min":28,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Jorgen in Stormwind City.\nLetter to Jorgen\nProvided: Letter to Jorgen","desc":"Recently a diplomat was sent to Theramore to meet with Jaina Proudmoore. That diplomat never arrived.\nI believe the Defias are involved in this plot, but I'm not sure how. The diplomat's disappearance still eludes public attention, but it can't remain that way for long.\nAgents of the king are already scouring the city for clues, but I have my own contacts I would like involved.\nIn the Valley of Heroes is an old friend of mine named Jorgen. Find him, give him this note, and follow his instructions.","rew":"Experience: 230","back":"Hmph, you better have good reason to interrupt a man and his fishin'. I don't take kindly to peddlers, let alone beggars.","done":"Hmm... <Jorgen looks up at you through squinted eyes.>\nAll right. I'll help ya, but not because I want to, but because I'm obligated.\nAnd let's get one thing straight: you're knowin' far more than you should to begin with. Let's keep this our little secret, and don't go blabbin' at any taverns about anything you find out. Understand?","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":80.2,"y":44.1,"n":"Bishop DeLavey","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":76.3,"y":85.1,"n":"Jorgen","e":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"201":{"id":201,"t":"Investigate the Camp","lv":32,"min":28,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find the hunters' camp and report its location to Krazek in Booty Bay.\nFind the place the quest sends you to.","desc":"I've gotten reports of a group of hunters that have set up camp upriver of the Venture Company mining camp on Lake Nazferiti. Now, normally I wouldn't care, but improbably, I heard that Hemet Nesingwary was one of the hunters there. He's certainly well-connected, if you catch my meaning, and you never can be too safe.\nWhy don't you go check out the camp, ‹name›, see what they're about?","rew":"Money: 16 0 gold, 16 silver, 0 copper Experience: 260\n+50 reputation with Booty Bay\n-250 reputation with Bloodsail Buccaneers","back":"Well? Did you have any luck in locating the camp?","done":"Hmmm, so my information was correct, as usual. Interesting. Well, I don't suppose they pose any sort of threat of interference with our operation, but perhaps they have a need for some of our excellent manufactured products. Hmmm...","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":26.9,"y":77.2,"n":"Krazek","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"601":{"id":601,"t":"Water Elementals","lv":37,"min":32,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Acquire 6 Water Elemental Bracers for Baron Revilgaz in Booty Bay.\n6 Water Elemental Bracers Lesser Water Elemental 38 %","desc":"The water elementals were no doubt summoned by Gazban, the goblin wizard rumored to have discovered the Stone of the Tides. As you may know, the Stone of the Tides curses its bearer, causing him to fade in and out of existence...\nPerhaps we can find a way to counteract the curse. We can have a mage of Dalaran analyze the magical residue of one of the water elemental's bracers. I need you to go back to the island and retrieve a few specimens.","rew":"Money: 40 0 gold, 40 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,850\n+100 reputation with Booty Bay\n-500 reputation with Bloodsail Buccaneers","back":"Have you had any luck, ‹name›?","done":"Hm, I haven't the eye to examine these bracers to see if any of them will be of any use, but I'm sure at least one of them will be able to help. Take them to Dalaran and have a mage look at them.\nAfter all, I can't very well leave Booty Bay just to chat with those tiresome old mages.\nNot that I'm worried anyone would try to elbow their way into being the new baron. No one crosses Revilgaz and lives to tell of it.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":27.2,"y":76.9,"n":"Baron Revilgaz","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"3721":{"id":3721,"t":"An OOX of Your Own","lv":50,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 40 instead of 45.","rew":"You will receive:\nMechanical Chicken\nExperience: 7,100\n+200 reputation with Booty Bay\n-1,000 reputation with Bloodsail Buccaneers","done":"You've recovered three of my OOX homing robots! You've gone above and beyond what you needed to, so I will give you something special for all your help. It is a miniature version of the very same robot that you have come to know and love, the OOX!\nI normally wouldn't let anyone have such a potentially lethal device, but you've been a real help. Besides - the combat mechanisms and the homing logic on this one have been disabled.\nOther than that, it's an OOX by golly!","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":28.4,"y":76.4,"n":"Oglethorpe Obnoticus","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"8201":{"id":8201,"t":"A Collection of Heads","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 9,950 experience instead of 14,500, 0.69 times as much.","obj":"String 5 Channeler's Heads, then return the Collection of Troll Heads to Exzhal on Yojamba Isle.\nGurubashi Head Collection\nProvided: Sacred Cord","desc":"It is true. Hakkar now dwells in Zul'Gurub, bathing in the power of our gods. Enthralled high priests now channel the energies of our most sacred divinities into the Soulflayer, who will soon have a strength beyond any being of Azeroth. He must be stopped!\nTake this sacred cord, and string through it the heads of the high priests responsible for channeling our gods' energy.\nWhen you have done this, return to me.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nBelt of Shrunken Heads Belt of Shriveled Heads Belt of Preserved Heads Belt of Tiny Heads\nMoney: 2 70 2 gold, 70 silver, 0 copper Experience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"Do you have the collection of heads, ‹name›? We must stop Hakkar from gaining more power!","done":"You gained the heads! You have halted the plundering of our gods' power, and weakened Hakkar!\nYour actions are truly heroic, ‹name›. May the heads of these troll thralls plead to you for mercy long after their blood chills.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":15.3,"y":15.5,"n":"Exzhal","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"841":{"id":841,"t":"Another Power Source?","lv":46,"min":38,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 10 Wastewander Water Pouches to Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle in Gadgetzan in exchange for another power source.\n10 Wastewander Water Pouch Andre Firebeard 35 % , Wastewander Scofflaw 35 % , Wastewander Assassin 35 % , Wastewander Bandit 35 % and 3 more","desc":"Let me guess - you didn't get whatever world-ending, nefarious deed you were doing done in time. No wait, better still... you dropped it in the sand! Well, whatever the reason, I do have additional power sources I will sell to you. This time, however, it will cost you ten, YES TEN Wastewander Water Pouches!\nTimes are tough all around, ‹name›, and power sources don't grow on trees! Hrm, but what if they did. Maybe we could MAKE a power source tree...","rew":"You will receive:\nModel 4711-FTZ Power Source","back":"Well, have you got the ten water pouches?","done":"Very well, here is another power source. I highly recommend you using it properly this time, unless you are eager to spend ten more water pouches for another water source.","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":52.5,"y":28.5,"n":"Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"3161":{"id":3161,"t":"Gahz'ridian","lv":48,"min":43,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Marvon Rivetseeker in Tanaris wants you to collect 30 Gahz'ridian Ornaments.\n30 Gahz'ridian Ornament Gahz'ridian\nGahz'ridian Detector\nProvided: Gahz'ridian Detector","desc":"‹name›, I'm a scientist, but also a treasure hunter at heart!\nLong ago, when trolls used to occupy this land, they created large amounts of ornaments modeled after Gahz'rilla, a hydra they worshipped as a deity. These ornaments are carved out of an element that I call \"Gahz'ridian\", after the hydra god.\nI did find some myself, but I'd like to have some more to study -- maybe you can find some?\nI even invented a detector that makes finding the Gahz'ridian a snap! Just put it on, and the search begins!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nSurveyor's Tunic Staff of Lore\nExperience: 4,400\n+100 reputation with Gadgetzan","back":"Are you having any trouble?\nYou can find Gahz'ridian just about anywhere in Tanaris, ‹name›, so keep looking!","done":"Perfect; these ornaments are perfect for my studies. Thanks so much for the help, ‹name›.\nOh, can I get my helmet back?","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":52.7,"y":45.9,"n":"Marvon Rivetseeker","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"5801":{"id":5801,"t":"Fire Plume Forged","lv":57,"min":55,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Skeleton Key Mold and 2 Thorium Bars to the top of Fire Plume Ridge in Un'Goro Crater. Use the Skeleton Key Mold by the lava lake to forge the Unfinished Skeleton Key.\nBring the Unfinished Skeleton Key to Alchemist Arbington at Chillwind Point, Western Plaguelands.\nUnfinished Skeleton Key\nProvided: Skeleton Key Mold","desc":"You need two bars of thorium and a powerfully hot heat source to forge the key stem. You're on your own for the thorium, but I can help with the heat.\nTo our west in Un'Goro Crater is Fire Plume Ridge - a simmering volcano. The lava lake up top is hot enough to fuse thorium and bone together. Your gold has bought you a mold that simply requires you to dip it in the lake up top; the lava will take care of the rest.\nThat's it on my end. To finish your key, you'll need to talk to Arbington again.","rew":"Experience: 4,500","back":"Do you have the stem of the skeletal key finished? I'm truly sorry you had to bear the brunt of the fee to purchase the mold, but we must all do our part to counter the Scourge. Once you hand me the unfinished key, you'll be ready for the final item needed to complete its construction.\nIt won't be easy at all, but the work you've done to date in preparing for an assault on Andorhal will now start to pay for itself. You'll see.","done":"We've got quite the costly skeleton key there, don't we ‹name›? Still, it remains unfinished; the time has now come to put some focus behind our creation. To that end, you're going to have to face the ultimate foe we've been working towards facing in Andorhal... the being that runs the show within the ruined city walls.\nI'm speaking of Araj the Summoner - a lich, and one of the most powerful beings the Scourge calls as its own.\nTanaris Western Plaguelands Un'Goro Crater","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":51.5,"y":28.8,"n":"Krinkle Goodsteel","s":1},{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":42.7,"y":83.8,"n":"Alchemist Arbington","e":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"8921":{"id":8921,"t":"The Ectoplasmic Distiller","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays -40g instead of 0.","obj":"Return to Mux Manascrambler in Gadgetzan with 1 Delicate Arcanite Converter, 4 Greater Eternal Essence, 10 Stonescale Oil, 25 Volcanic Ash and 40 gold.\nDelicate Arcanite Converter\n4 Greater Eternal Essence\n10 Stonescale Oil\n25 Volcanic Ash Volcanic Ash","desc":"Ah, you're in need of my latest project... the extra-dimensional ghost revealer! Unfortunately I've run out of funds and manpower.\nYou're willing to help? Excellent! Our first task is to build a device to harvest the very fabric of death! Building an ectoplasmic distiller won't be an easy task, ‹name›.\nI'll need you to bring me an arcanite converter, some greater eternal essences and stonescale oil. I'll also need some volcanic ash from the lava pools in the Burning Steppes to build a filter.","rew":"You will receive:\nMux's Quality Goods\nExperience: 6,600","back":"I understand the materials are a bit pricey... but I promise you every last one of them shall be necessary!","done":"These are precisely the materials I needed. Quite timely too, ‹name›!\nIn mere moments I will have your distiller ready to go! In the meantime, take this as a reward for aiding me in my project.\nTanaris Un'Goro Crater","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":52.5,"y":27.2,"n":"Mux Manascrambler","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"8761":{"id":8761,"t":"The Grand Invoker","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Signet Ring of the Bronze Dragonflight","rew":"You will receive:\nSignet Ring of the Bronze Dragonflight\nExperience: 9,950\n+100 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"Never have I seen such tenacity! The Bronze Flight grants you one final enchantment. The Timeless One himself has requested it so!\nHand me your signet ring so that I may make the necessary adjustments.","done":"Rise, Grand Invoker! Rise and be recognized!","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":65.3,"y":50,"n":"Anachronos","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"921":{"id":921,"t":"Crown of the Earth","lv":5,"min":3,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Fill the Crystal Phial and bring it back to Tenaron Stormgrip atop Aldrassil.\nFilled Crystal Phial\nProvided: Crystal Phial","desc":"It is time for you to set out to seek your destiny, ‹name›. But before you are ready to set out into the world beyond our enchanted forests, there is much you must learn about our recent history.\nMuch has changed with our people since the Battle of Mount Hyjal. Nordrassil lies a pale shadow of what it once was, its power used to defeat Archimonde and drive back the Burning Legion...\nThere is a task you must perform. Go to the moonwell north of Aldrassil and return me a phial of its water.","rew":"Experience: 340\n+75 reputation with Darnassus","back":"The moonwells hold the waters of the Well of Eternity, the ancient source of magic that has wrought so many horrors upon our world.\nThe druids take advantage of its properties, and the Sentinels revere the wells as shrines to Elune, but sorcery is forbidden to all.","done":"So you have heard the first part of the aftermath of the Battle of Mount Hyjal. There is much more to be told and the task you have begun here will continue through the rest of your journey through Teldrassil and into Darnassus.","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":59.1,"y":39.4,"n":"Tenaron Stormgrip","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["teldrassil"]},"6361":{"id":6361,"t":"A Bundle of Hides","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Bundle of Hides to the wind rider master Devrak in the Crossroads.\nBundle of Hides\nProvided: Bundle of Hides","desc":"I have a bundle of hides from the animals of the Barrens, and must get them to Thunder Bluff. A colleague there, Ahanu, will use the hides to create leather goods.\nWill you take the hides to him for me?\nThe quickest way to Thunder Bluff is on the back of a wind rider. Bring the bundle of hides to Devrak, our wind rider master in the Crossroads, and speak to him about transport to Thunder Bluff.","rew":"Experience: 210\n+25 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"Are you here for a wind rider? You have something to transport?","done":"If you must take these hides to Thunder Bluff, then you are speaking to the right orc!","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":51.2,"y":29,"n":"Jahan Hawkwing","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":51.5,"y":30.3,"n":"Devrak","e":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"4921":{"id":4921,"t":"Lost in Battle","lv":20,"min":14,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Mankrik's wife and then return to him in the Crossroads.\nFind Mankrik's Wife","desc":"We battled in a small tauren camp when we were separated--she held three of the Bristlebacks off by herself. But the odds began to overwhelm us. I led some away only to see her overwhelmed by newcomers. In my rage, I turned to face my enemies, but they brought me down easily with their vast numbers.\nI awoke to a tauren druid tending my wounds--he had come across me on the Gold Road as I fell.\nPlease, ‹class›, find some sign of my wife.","rew":"Money: 9 0 gold, 9 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,150\n+75 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Have you found any sign of her at all? The pain in my chest tells me that the worst has happened, but I have hope you will find her safe and sound.","done":"I understand. Thank you, ‹class›.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":52,"y":31.6,"n":"Mankrik","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"4841":{"id":4841,"t":"Pacify the Centaur","lv":25,"min":23,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 12 Galak Scouts, 10 Galak Wranglers, and 6 Galak Windchasers, and then return to Cliffwatcher Longhorn in Freewind Post.\nGalak Scout slain : 0/ 12\nGalak Wrangler slain : 0/ 10\nGalak Windchaser slain : 0/ 6","desc":"‹name›, I entreat you to hunt these centaur down. They shall feel the wrath of our revenge. Attack the centaur camp to the north of Freewind Post! Let wrath guide your hand!","rew":"Money: 18 0 gold, 18 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,000\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"Come now ‹name›, I know you haven't killed your share yet. Hunt them down, and I shall give you a reward for my gratitude.","done":"For my gratitude, this is for you, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":45.7,"y":50.7,"n":"Cliffwatcher Longhorn","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["thousand-needles"]},"5481":{"id":5481,"t":"Gordo's Task","lv":5,"min":5,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Collect 3 Gloom Weed and deliver them to Junior Apothecary Holland in the Brill graveyard.\n3 Gloom Weed Gloom Weed","desc":"Master want weeds. Us gots big hands and not good at picking. You help us and we not hurt you. Us need gloom weed. Many weeds around here and near road.\nWhen you have gloom weed you take to Master Holland in Brill graveyard.","rew":"Experience: 230\n+50 reputation with Undercity","back":"Where's that useless abomination? Either you have what I need or you'd best get out there and find it.","done":"What's this? Gloom weed?! I've no need for gloom weed! That mindless mass of flesh is out there picking daisies and convincing the Lady knows how many dupes like you into doing the same. No offense.\nVery well, you're here now and that's all that matters. Since I'm not going to bother to try to explain things to that abomination how about you collect what I really need... doom weed!","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":43.1,"y":54.7,"n":"Gordo","s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":57.4,"y":48.8,"n":"Junior Apothecary Holland","e":1}],"cats":["tirisfal-glades"]},"361":{"id":361,"t":"A Letter Undelivered","lv":7,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Yvette Farthing, and deliver to her the letter from Thurman Agamand.\nThurman's Letter\nProvided: Thurman's Letter","desc":"This is a letter written by Thurman, the eldest son of Gregor Agamand. It is addressed to an Yvette Farthing, though it does not appear to have reached her...","rew":"Experience: 480\n+75 reputation with Undercity","back":"Yes?","done":"Oh...my poor Thurman! I begged him to leave Agamand Mills with me and my father, but his family loyalty was too strong! And I knew it! I just knew it that Brand meant him harm!! Oh, curse this Plague, and the Scourge!\n<Yvette's face then smoothes and grows cold.>\nBut regrets are for the weak. As a Forsaken, I have new goals and love is not one of them. I would thank you for delivering this letter, for I had wondered what happened to my past love.\nBut that life is over. Forever.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":61.6,"y":52.6,"n":"Yvette Farthing","e":1}],"cats":["tirisfal-glades"]},"2201":{"id":2201,"t":"Find the Gems","lv":43,"min":37,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 37 instead of 40.","obj":"Find the ruby, sapphire, and topaz that are scattered throughout Uldaman. Once acquired, contact Talvash del Kissel remotely by using the Phial of Scrying he previously gave you.\nFrom the journal, you know...\n* The ruby has been stashed in a barricaded Shadowforge area.\n* The topaz has been hidden in an urn in one of the Trogg areas, near some Alliance dwarves.\n* The sapphire has been claimed by Grimlok, the trogg leader.\nShattered Necklace Ruby Shadowforge Cache\nShattered Necklace Sapphire Grimlok\nShattered Necklace Topaz Conspicuous Urn\nProvided: Bloodstained Journal","desc":"The paladin's journal has provided perhaps the only clues that Uldaman will yield as to the location of the necklace's gems. If the paladin's scribing remains accurate, then the Shadowforge dwarves and the troggs that vie for control of the dig site will need to be dealt with.\nArmed with this knowledge, the search for the gems begins in earnest. When all the gems have been acquired, Talvash in Ironforge should be notified via the Phial of Scrying as per his instructions.","rew":"Experience: 3,600","back":"Talvash's image comes into focus from the waters of the scrying bowl.\n\"Wow, you're still alive! Did you manage to find the gems? Are you truly the savior of my reputation I have hoped for? Please tell me you didn't waste a charge on the phial just to chat; those things are NOT cheap, and I'm already in dire financial straits.\"","done":"Yep, those indeed are the three gems. Good job! Unfortunately, your work isn't quite over just yet.\nNo, I'm not trying to pull a fast one here, silly ‹class›. This is about making magic jewelry - Talvash del Kissel quality-level jewelry! You need a strong power source to give it some oomph. Well, that necklace has no more oomph to give.\nStart Remains of a Paladin End Talvash's Scrying Bowl Level 43 , requires level 37 Difficulty 37 39 41 46 54 Side Alliance Type Dungeon Shareable No Quest ID 2201\nThe chain\n6 quests from level 41 to 44, 18,425 XP in all.\n1 [ 41 ] The Shattered Necklace\nSearch for the original creator of the shattered necklace to learn of its potential value.\nShattered Necklace\n3,300 XP\n2 [ 41 ] Lore for a Price\nBring five silver bars to Talvash del Kissel in Ironforge.\nTalvash del Kissel Dun Morogh\n2,450 XP\n3 [ 42 ] Back to Uldaman\nSearch for clues as to the current disposition of Talvash's necklace within Uldaman.\nTalvash del Kissel Dun Morogh\n2,550 XP\n4 [ 43 ] Find the Gems this quest\nFind the ruby, sapphire, and topaz that are scattered throughout Uldaman.\nRemains of a Paladin\n3,600 XP\n5 [ 44 ] Restoring the Necklace\nObtain a power source from the most powerful construct you can find in Uldaman, and deliver it to Talvash del Kissel in Ironforge.\nTalvash's Scrying Bowl\n925 XP\n6 [ 44 ] Restoring the Necklace\nTalvash del Kissel Dun Morogh\n5,600 XP","cats":["uldaman"]},"2361":{"id":2361,"t":"Restoring the Necklace","lv":44,"min":37,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nTalvash's Enhancing Necklace\nExperience: 5,600\n+200 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","done":"I gladly give you this necklace, mighty ‹class›. You have done me an invaluable service, and for that I thank you. Wear it with pride, and make sure you mention loudly and repeatedly who made it for you!\nAlso, if you could toss in the fact that it really isn't cursed, that would be great.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":56.9,"y":21.7,"n":"Talvash del Kissel","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["uldaman"]},"3881":{"id":3881,"t":"Expedition Salvation","lv":53,"min":48,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 5,250 experience instead of 4,200, 1.25 times as much.","obj":"Bring a Crate of Foodstuffs and Research Equipment to Williden Marshal in Un'Goro Crater.\nCrate of Foodstuffs Crate of Foodstuffs , Research Equipment , Crate of Foodstuffs\nResearch Equipment Research Equipment","desc":"I don't know how you made it here, but you're a sight for sore eyes! I'm Williden Marshal, and I lead a non-aligned expedition troupe. Our latest and greatest endeavor has met with what seems like countless disasters, the most serious of which being that we underestimated the savagery of Un'Goro Crater!\nAs we fled our base camps in the southwestern and northeastern parts of the crater, we left behind vital supplies. You look like you're capable enough - can you help us by getting them back?","rew":"Money: 40 0 gold, 40 silver, 0 copper Experience: 5,250","back":"If we're going to have any chance of getting out of here alive, we'll need our big crate of foodstuffs. Also, getting at least some of our research equipment back would be a blessing in a sea of misery.","done":"You got both our foodstuff AND our research equipment back! You've not only saved the expedition, you've also saved our lives. I and the rest of my team can't thank you enough; we just might make it here for a while now thanks to you.\nWhile we don't have much, I'm certainly not going to leave you high and dry for the invaluable help you've given us. Thank you, ‹name› - you've got a friend in Marshal Expeditions!","pins":[{"z":"Un'Goro Crater","x":43.9,"y":7.1,"n":"Williden Marshal","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ungoro-crater"]},"3961":{"id":3961,"t":"Linken's Adventure","lv":54,"min":47,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Silver Totem of Aquementas to Linken in Marshal's Refuge.\nSilver Totem of Aquementas\nProvided: Silver Totem of Aquementas","desc":"To think all this time that the reason Linken came here was to rid us of Blazerunner... He seems like such an ordinary guy, but I did notice that he's not at all interested in any of my experiments or gadgets like most gnomes would be. He must be a true warrior at heart.\nBring the totem to him. See if that helps him remember why he came here.","rew":"Experience: 2,700","back":"Hi, again, ‹name›!","done":"Did J.D. help you at all?","pins":[{"z":"Un'Goro Crater","x":41.9,"y":2.7,"n":"J.D. Collie","s":1},{"z":"Un'Goro Crater","x":44.7,"y":8.1,"n":"Linken","e":1}],"cats":["ungoro-crater"]},"5961":{"id":5961,"t":"The Champion of the Banshee Queen","lv":56,"min":54,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Nathanos Blightcaller in the Eastern Plaguelands. He is said to have taken up residence at the Marris Stead.","desc":"It pleases me greatly to see the battle hardened join our cause. Our numbers grow in size and strength as each day passes. Perhaps you are prepared to test your mettle, ‹class›?\nAmong the first of my champions was Nathanos, now known as the Blightcaller. Few exist with more dedication or vigor amidst our ranks.\nSeek him out in the Eastern Plaguelands. He resides at the Marris Stead; occasionally roaming the decimated wastes, slaying all Scourge and Alliance filth that cross his path.","rew":"Experience: 1,450\n+25 reputation with Undercity","done":"Surely the Dark Lady does not believe you worthy to meet her champion. You are here to feed my hounds, yes? There could be no other reason for this interruption.\nUndercity Eastern Plaguelands","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":58.1,"y":91.8,"n":"Lady Sylvanas Windrunner","s":1},{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":22.2,"y":63.5,"n":"Nathanos Blightcaller","e":1}],"cats":["undercity"]},"3001":{"id":3001,"t":"Seeking Strahad","lv":30,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Strahad Farsan in Ratchet.","desc":"I have taught you skills in the past, but the time has come for another to teach you. He is in Ratchet, and his name is Strahad. He is human, but do not let that fool you into thinking he is weak, nor is he your enemy... at least for now. He is powerful and should be respected. He can teach you about greater summonings, summonings I feel you are prepared for. Go to him now.\nYou can find him in Ratchet... above the port town next to the tower there.","rew":"Experience: 600","done":"A busy day in Ratchet, isn't it? How I enjoy watching the toil of a port city. So much mystery, so much adventure... so much ignorance.\nIs that hatred I see in your eyes, ‹name›? Good, we will put that to good use.\nUndercity The Barrens","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":85.1,"y":26,"n":"Carendin Halgar","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.6,"y":35.5,"n":"Strahad Farsan","e":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"1801":{"id":1801,"t":"Tome of the Cabal","lv":30,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Jorah Annison in the Undercity.","desc":"It will take more than a simple summoning circle to bring forth a felhunter for you to challenge.\nMy three acolytes and I will assist in creating the magic circles. You require a copy of the Tome of the Cabal, which has been lost to us for some time. It was written by the first group of warlocks to summon a felhunter unaided.\nPerhaps Jorah Annison can help you with this. He's employed as a cartographer in the Undercity these days, but still knows more of ancient texts than any I know.","rew":"Experience: 600","done":"Map making! Pictures, estimations of reality. I have no use for such things.\nIn books, narrative, description! That is where truth lies. I would trade all the maps in this store for one book on the rise of necromancy, or a tale of the Dark Lady's triumph.\nThe Barrens Undercity","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.6,"y":35.5,"n":"Strahad Farsan","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":75.9,"y":37.9,"n":"Jorah Annison","e":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"5401":{"id":5401,"t":"Argent Dawn Commission","lv":55,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nArgent Dawn Commission\nExperience: 550\n+10 reputation with Argent Dawn","done":"All who fight evil on behalf of the Argent Dawn must don our commission. Wearing such will earn your right to claim rewards our quartermasters have to offer.\nWhile under commission, you'll be able to acquire Scourgestones from slain Scourge; these are marks of insignia that they sometimes possess. Procure these insignia and bring them to me. For each set you turn in, you will receive our marker of heroism - the Argent Dawn Valor Token.\nAchieve your destiny, ‹class› - join the fight today!","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":43,"y":83.5,"n":"Argent Officer Pureheart","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"6281":{"id":6281,"t":"Continue to Stormwind","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Buy a gryphon ride from the gryphon master Thor, then bring Lewis' Note to Osric Strang, in the shop Limited Immunity, in the Old Town of Stormwind.\nLewis' Note\nProvided: Lewis' Note","desc":"For a small fee, you can take a gryphon to Stormwind, so you can deliver Lewis' note to Osric. You won't get there faster any other way.\nIf that sounds acceptable, then just speak to me again when you're ready for the ride. I'll charge you a little, but trust me; it'll be worth it!","rew":"Money: 1 75 0 gold, 1 silver, 75 copper Experience: 420\n+50 reputation with Stormwind","back":"You've been traveling, eh? Have you been anywhere interesting?","done":"Ah, a note from Quartermaster Lewis? I'm not surprised he needs more gear. Sentinel Hill is far away, in a land Stormwind has all but forgotten.\nWell thank you, ‹name›. Here's some money to cover your travel costs.\nWestfall Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Westfall","x":56.6,"y":52.6,"n":"Thor","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":77.2,"y":61,"n":"Osric Strang","e":1}],"cats":["westfall"]},"281":{"id":281,"t":"Reclaiming Goods","lv":25,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Search the crates and barrels at the coastal Murloc camps.","desc":"Not long ago a merchant vessel, the Blind Princess, was raided by Murlocs. Although the ship escaped intact, much of its cargo was dragged overboard by the creatures, including a very valuable statuette of Terenas Menethil. We want that statuette recovered.\nSearch the coastal Murloc hovels for crates, barrels and other evidence of lost cargo. Find the Menethil Statuette and return it to me.","rew":"You will receive:\n5 Healing Potion\nExperience: 500\n+25 reputation with Stormwind","done":"This crate is covered with clawed scratches, and the marks of water damage. Prying it open reveals soggy and rotted straw, as if something of value was stored in the crate. You search through the straw...\n...and find a an armload of red-colored bottles.","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":8.3,"y":58.6,"n":"Karl Boran","s":1},{"z":"Wetlands","x":13.5,"y":41.4,"n":"Damaged Crate","e":1}],"cats":["wetlands"]},"5161":{"id":5161,"t":"Wrath of the Blue Flight","lv":60,"min":57,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Haleh if you wish to continue.","desc":"We understand what the cursed brood of Deathwing attempts to do and we know that it cannot be allowed.\nBecause of the protection Blackrock mountain affords Nefarian, it has become increasingly difficult for us to intercede.\nWe can, however, empower you, mortal - should you so choose.\nThe path before you is one full of peril. You must decide whether to accept our help. Ponder this and speak with me again when a decision has been made.","rew":"Experience: 650","done":"So it shall be...","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":54.5,"y":51.2,"n":"Haleh","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["winterspring"]},"8041":{"id":8041,"t":"Strength of Mount Mugamba","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 58 instead of 60.","rew":"You will receive:\nStrength of Mugamba\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","done":"Hail, ‹class›. I am Jin'rokh the Breaker, troll of Mugamba. We of the Zandalar tribe recognize your accomplishments. We salute your tenacity and strength of will.\nWear this talisman around your neck, ‹class›. Let the strength of Mount Mugamba flow through your being. Be empowered as you strike down our enemies!","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":15.3,"y":14.4,"n":"Jin'rokh the Breaker","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zulgurub"]}});